1
00:00:00,095 --> 00:00:02,657
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:08,670
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:10,067 --> 00:00:13,027
اللهم الشرح الصدرك وارنا ألحق يا أرحم الراحمين ،

4
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:17,331
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ

5
00:00:18,024 --> 00:00:25,238
The next section is the longest continuous section, where Shaikh(شيخ) Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) talks.

6
00:00:26,095 --> 00:00:33,436
This is an advice to the ones, who stay behind.

7
00:00:35,084 --> 00:00:41,586
It’s a wonderful Naseeha(نَصيحة) that he gives to the ones, who miss out on Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

8
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:51,523
He says: Oh, you who have neglected Jihad(جهاد) and stayed away from the path of success.

9
00:00:53,143 --> 00:00:57,438
You have put yourself in the position of exclusion from the mercy of Allah.

10
00:00:58,924 --> 00:01:02,269
You have deprived yourself from the greatest reward.

11
00:01:04,553 --> 00:01:06,371
What is it that caused you to stay behind?

12
00:01:07,721 --> 00:01:10,393
Why haven't you joined the ranks of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين)?

13
00:01:11,447 --> 00:01:14,308
Why are you holding back your soul and your wealth?

14
00:01:16,043 --> 00:01:18,168
It must be one of the following reasons.

15
00:01:19,661 --> 00:01:21,287
1) The desire to live a long life.

16
00:01:22,899 --> 00:01:27,257
2) The attachment to family, wealth, or friends.

17
00:01:27,496 --> 00:01:30,433
3)The desire to do more good deeds before fighting Jihad(جهاد).

18
00:01:31,568 --> 00:01:33,625
4) The love of a beautiful wife.

19
00:01:34,704 --> 00:01:39,625
5) Your position of power or love of a comfortable lifestyle.

20
00:01:40,473 --> 00:01:42,138
Nothing else could be holding you back.

21
00:01:43,479 --> 00:01:48,436
It must be one of the above mentioned reasons that is keeping you away from Allah.

22
00:01:49,132 --> 00:01:52,190
Can’t you hear the call of Allah directed at you:

23
00:01:52,331 --> 00:02:04,819
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا ما لَكُم إِذا قيلَ لَكُمُ انفِروا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ اثّاقَلتُم إِلَى الأَرضِ ۚ

24
00:02:05,813 --> 00:02:11,371
أَرَضيتُم بِالحَياةِ الدُّنيا مِنَ الآخِرَةِ ۚ

25
00:02:11,935 --> 00:02:18,956
فَما مَتاعُ الحَياةِ الدُّنيا فِي الآخِرَةِ إِلّا قَليلٌ۞

26
00:02:19,621 --> 00:02:25,379
Oh, you have believed! What is the matter with you that, when you are told to go forth in the cause of Allah,

27
00:02:25,772 --> 00:02:27,563
you adhere heavily to the earth.

28
00:02:28,524 --> 00:02:32,536
Are you satisfied with the life of this world rather than the Hereafter?

29
00:02:33,181 --> 00:02:38,316
But what is the enjoyment of worldly life compared to the hereafter except a very little.

30
00:02:40,238 --> 00:02:47,761
Listen carefully to how I respond to each and every one of the causes, that are holding you back from Jihad(جهاد),

31
00:02:48,824 --> 00:02:51,361
you will then come to realize that you are deprived,

32
00:02:51,978 --> 00:02:55,975
and you would learn that it is nothing but yourself and Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ)

33
00:02:56,348 --> 00:02:58,619
that is preventing you from Jihad(جهاد);

34
00:03:00,056 --> 00:03:02,821
 1) Number One: The desire to live longer:

35
00:03:03,511 --> 00:03:08,164
In the name of Allah fearlessness does not decrease your life.

36
00:03:09,414 --> 00:03:11,224
And cowardice does not increase it.

37
00:03:12,731 --> 00:03:13,665
Allah says:

38
00:03:13,962 --> 00:03:17,375
وَلِكُلِّ أُمَّةٍ أَجَلٌ ۖ

39
00:03:17,875 --> 00:03:28,303
فَإِذا جاءَ أَجَلُهُم لا يَستَأخِرونَ ساعَةً ۖ وَلا يَستَقدِمونَ۞

40
00:03:29,004 --> 00:03:31,277
 And for every nation is a specified term.

41
00:03:32,011 --> 00:03:37,503
So when their time has come, they will not remain behind an hour, nor will they proceed it.

42
00:03:38,212 --> 00:03:40,361
This is in Al-Araf(ألأعراف) Verse 34.

43
00:03:41,777 --> 00:03:42,842
And Allah says:

44
00:03:43,168 --> 00:03:55,281
وَلَن يُؤَخِّرَ اللَّهُ نَفسًا إِذا جاءَ أَجَلُها ۚ وَاللَّهُ خَبيرٌ بِما تَعمَلونَ۞

45
00:03:57,528 --> 00:04:00,916
But never will Allah delay a soul when it's time has come.

46
00:04:01,393 --> 00:04:03,266
And Allah is acquainted with what you do.

47
00:04:03,511 --> 00:04:05,609
And that’s in Al-Munafiqoon(ألمنافقون) verse 11.

48
00:04:06,426 --> 00:04:07,594
And Allah says:

49
00:04:08,177 --> 00:04:17,679
كُلُّ نَفسٍ ذائِقَةُ المَوتِ ۖ ثُمَّ إِلَينا تُرجَعونَ۞

50
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:22,948
Every soul will taste death, then to us, you will be returned.

51
00:04:23,943 --> 00:04:25,582
And this is in Al-Ankabut(ألعنكبوت), Verse 57.

52
00:04:27,292 --> 00:04:31,692
And then he says: Oh, you have deceived yourself!

53
00:04:32,322 --> 00:04:35,397
Remember that during death, there's agony and pain.

54
00:04:36,185 --> 00:04:38,300
And on the Day of Judgment, there's great fear.

55
00:04:39,153 --> 00:04:41,664
Do you remember that a Shaheed(شَهِيد) is spared from all of this.

56
00:04:43,865 --> 00:04:47,524
He does not feel the pain of death, except like a sting of an insect.

57
00:04:49,074 --> 00:04:51,396
My brother, why miss out on this opportunity.

58
00:04:52,199 --> 00:04:55,334
And then after death, you would be spared from the punishment of the grave.

59
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,752
You will not go through the questioning of the angels in the grave.

60
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:02,918
And you will be tranquil on the day of judgment, when everybody else is horrified.

61
00:05:03,496 --> 00:05:09,404
After your death your soul will be in the Inside of birds flying in paradise.

62
00:05:10,237 --> 00:05:13,414
Can you see the difference between dying a natural death and being a Shaheed(شَهِيد)?

63
00:05:14,408 --> 00:05:17,175
2) Number two: Attachment to family:

64
00:05:17,963 --> 00:05:22,899
If what prevents you from Jihad(جهاد) is family, wealth and friends, Then; Allah says:

65
00:05:23,983 --> 00:05:35,261
وَما أَموالُكُم وَلا أَولادُكُم بِالَّتي تُقَرِّبُكُم عِندَنا زُلفىٰ

66
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:45,487
 بِالَّتي تُقَرِّبُكُم عِندَنا زُلفىٰ إِلّا مَن آمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صالِحًا

67
00:05:46,439 --> 00:05:56,472
 فَأُولٰئِكَ لَهُم جَزاءُ الضِّعفِ بِما عَمِلوا وَهُم فِي الغُرُفاتِ آمِنونَ۞

68
00:05:57,481 --> 00:06:01,381
And it is not your wealth or your children that brings you nearer to us in position,

69
00:06:02,315 --> 00:06:06,820
but it is by being one, who has believed and done righteousness.

70
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:09,353
So these things don't really bring you closer to Allah.

71
00:06:11,055 --> 00:06:23,503
اعلَموا أَنَّمَا الحَياةُ الدُّنيا لَعِبٌ وَلَهوٌ وَزينَةٌ وَتَفاخُرٌ بَينَكُم

72
00:06:24,132 --> 00:06:31,862
 وَتَفاخُرٌ بَينَكُم وَتَكاثُرٌ فِي الأَموالِ وَالأَولادِ ۖ

73
00:06:32,485 --> 00:06:41,501
كَمَثَلِ غَيثٍ أَعجَبَ الكُفّارَ نَباتُهُ ثُمَّ يَهيجُ فَتَراهُ مُصفَرًّا

74
00:06:41,991 --> 00:06:49,116
ثُمَّ يَهيجُ فَتَراهُ مُصفَرًّا ثُمَّ يَكونُ حُطامًا ۖ

75
00:06:49,512 --> 00:06:58,417
وَفِي الآخِرَةِ عَذابٌ شَديدٌ وَمَغفِرَةٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضوانٌ ۚ

76
00:06:58,862 --> 00:07:05,803
وَمَا الحَياةُ الدُّنيا إِلّا مَتاعُ الغُرورِ۞

77
00:07:05,943 --> 00:07:08,479
Know that the life of this world is, but amusement

78
00:07:08,704 --> 00:07:12,732
and diversion, and adornment and boasting to one another,

79
00:07:13,169 --> 00:07:16,148
and competition in the increase of wealth and children.

80
00:07:16,829 --> 00:07:21,521
Like the example of a rain whose plant growth pleases the tillers,

81
00:07:22,011 --> 00:07:25,790
 then it dries and you see it turned yellow, then it becomes debris.

82
00:07:26,382 --> 00:07:30,454
And in the Hereafter is a severe punishment and forgiveness from Allah and approval.

83
00:07:30,772 --> 00:07:34,414
And what is the worldly life except the enjoyment of delusion.

84
00:07:34,705 --> 00:07:36,264
That’s Surah Al-Hadid(سورة ألحديد) verse 20.

85
00:07:39,056 --> 00:07:40,402
The Messenger of Allah said:

86
00:07:41,215 --> 00:07:48,357
And the area under a whip, or under your foot in Paradise is better than the world and everything in it.

87
00:07:49,506 --> 00:07:50,233
That's in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

88
00:07:51,407 --> 00:07:55,803
So does it make sense to leave this vast Kingdom in paradise for the sake of your family,

89
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,646
who in a short while will be among the dead.

90
00:07:59,028 --> 00:08:03,928
A family that might Express towards you animosity, bad behavior or jealousy.

91
00:08:05,064 --> 00:08:06,633
If you are wealthy, they love you.

92
00:08:06,979 --> 00:08:08,546
If you're broke, they forsake you.

93
00:08:09,291 --> 00:08:12,300
One day they are with you, and the next day against you.

94
00:08:13,149 --> 00:08:16,040
In the end, on the day of judgment, they will leave you alone,

95
00:08:16,495 --> 00:08:19,491
and they would hold you accountable for even the size of a grain.

96
00:08:20,698 --> 00:08:25,642
They would all desire that they would be saved on that day,

97
00:08:25,822 --> 00:08:28,176
even if it is you that is going to hell fire.

98
00:08:28,421 --> 00:08:36,642
Allah سبحانه تعالى says that, on the day of judgment, a person would wish to sacrifice

99
00:08:36,734 --> 00:08:43,277
their wife, their children, their parents, their tribe and everyone in the earth,

100
00:08:43,622 --> 00:08:45,178
if it's going to save them from hellfire.

101
00:08:46,077 --> 00:08:52,395
3) Number Three: Love of wealth: If it is your wealth that is keeping you behind,

102
00:08:52,961 --> 00:08:56,797
then how can it do so, when you know that it will eventually leave you?

103
00:08:58,517 --> 00:09:00,849
See, the problem here is that you don't want to leave your wealth,

104
00:09:01,228 --> 00:09:02,562
 but your wealth is going to leave you.

105
00:09:03,839 --> 00:09:12,096
So why not leave it and get the Ajr(أجْر), rather than be forced, for it to leave you?

106
00:09:12,796 --> 00:09:17,396
And because of this wealth, you will be asked on the Day of Judgment: How did you make it and how did you spend it?

107
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:23,646
You will be asked these two questions on a day that would make a child gray headed, a day of horror.

108
00:09:24,463 --> 00:09:28,342
The Messenger of Allah said: The poor Muslims will proceed the rich in Paradise

109
00:09:28,641 --> 00:09:31,367
by half a day, 500 years.

110
00:09:32,658 --> 00:09:33,674
Allah says:

111
00:09:33,936 --> 00:09:40,190
إِنَّما أَموالُكُم وَأَولادُكُم فِتنَةٌ ۚ

112
00:09:40,496 --> 00:09:45,002
وَاللَّهُ عِندَهُ أَجرٌ عَظيمٌ۞

113
00:09:45,672 --> 00:09:47,896
Your wealth and your children are, but a trial.

114
00:09:48,441 --> 00:09:50,864
And Allah has with Him a great reward.

115
00:09:51,108 --> 00:09:52,729
At-Taghabagun(ألتغابن) Verse 15.

116
00:09:53,198 --> 00:09:58,999
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث) that the poor are among Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون).

117
00:09:59,691 --> 00:10:02,969
 There are many poor among Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون), they came out from Makkah.

118
00:10:03,599 --> 00:10:05,017
They had to leave everything behind them.

119
00:10:05,042 --> 00:10:08,647
Some of them were originally wealthy, but they became broke.

120
00:10:08,897 --> 00:10:14,162
Hijrah(هجرة) wasn't a very easy thing.

121
00:10:14,213 --> 00:10:15,385
They had to leave their wealth behind.

122
00:10:15,457 --> 00:10:16,598
For example, Suhaib
Al-Rumi(صهيب الرومي).

123
00:10:17,462 --> 00:10:20,504
Suhaib Al-Rumi(صهيب الرومي) is Roman, and he was a slave in Makkah.

124
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,842
But he did business in Makkah, and he became wealthy.

125
00:10:24,189 --> 00:10:26,227
He accumulated a lot of wealth, when he was in Makkah.

126
00:10:26,976 --> 00:10:27,802
He became Muslim.

127
00:10:29,563 --> 00:10:33,510
And when he went out in Hijrah(هجرة), some of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) pursued him.

128
00:10:34,956 --> 00:10:43,900
And he stood on a hill and he took an arrow from his quiver and he pointed towards him, and he said:

129
00:10:46,505 --> 00:10:52,009
You know that I'm among the best archers in Makkah.

130
00:10:53,029 --> 00:10:56,716
I'm going to empty my quiver in you If you don't leave me alone.

131
00:10:57,716 --> 00:10:58,356
Then he said:

132
00:10:58,444 --> 00:11:02,794
أتَيْتَنَا سَولُوكً فَسَارَ لَكَ بَيَنَ مالً وَاَهْل

133
00:11:04,294 --> 00:11:06,762
They said: You came to us in Makkah broke.

134
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:11,531
And you lived among us, and accumulated wealth.

135
00:11:12,028 --> 00:11:14,495
Now you want to leave and take your wealth with you.

136
00:11:14,916 --> 00:11:18,417
We're not going to let you go with your money.

137
00:11:20,925 --> 00:11:29,717
And I think in this story is a stark warning for Muslims, who are living in the West.

138
00:11:31,028 --> 00:11:32,636
Maybe one day the same thing will happen.

139
00:11:33,314 --> 00:11:37,931
You'll be told you came here broke and poor, and you became wealthy among us.

140
00:11:38,275 --> 00:11:40,114
You can’t just leave and take your money with you.

141
00:11:41,693 --> 00:11:46,828
So they told Suhaib(صهيب): Give us your money.

142
00:11:49,272 --> 00:11:50,022
He said: Fine!

143
00:11:50,304 --> 00:11:52,678
You will find my money in such and such place in Makkah.

144
00:11:55,258 --> 00:11:59,011
So he ransomed himself for them by giving them his wealth.

145
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:07,420
Suhaib(صهيب) arrived in Madina and as soon as Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him, he told him;

146
00:12:07,445 --> 00:12:09,325
ربَيهَ ألبَية أبى يحيى

147
00:12:10,115 --> 00:12:12,540
What a profitable trade, Abu Yahya(أبويحيى)!”

148
00:12:13,828 --> 00:12:16,044
 Without Suhaib(صهيب) telling him the story,

149
00:12:16,511 --> 00:12:20,323
the news was already with the Rasool Allah ﷺ and he told him: That was a profitable deal.

150
00:12:22,063 --> 00:12:25,442
You lost all of your money- and then he’s congratulated that it's a good deal,

151
00:12:26,005 --> 00:12:27,293
because it's really a good deal.

152
00:12:28,305 --> 00:12:29,838
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will give you more.

153
00:12:30,655 --> 00:12:32,403
So there are many poor among Al-Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

154
00:12:33,131 --> 00:12:40,172
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: These poor Muhajireen(مهاجرين) are going to knock on the gates of Jannah(جنة).

155
00:12:41,289 --> 00:12:44,210
 So the angels are going to open the gates and say: What are you doing here?

156
00:12:44,310 --> 00:12:46,448
Isn’t the day of judgment still going on?

157
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:49,609
The Hisab(حساب), proceedings of the Hisab(حساب) is still going on,

158
00:12:50,204 --> 00:12:53,488
and these Muhajireen(مهاجرين) are already knocking on the gates, they want to get in.

159
00:12:54,241 --> 00:12:58,175
So the angels are telling them? Didn’t you have to go through the reckoning?

160
00:12:58,781 --> 00:13:02,471
So the Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) said: We would be reckoned for what?

161
00:13:03,774 --> 00:13:09,166
All what we used to do, while we were living was carrying our swords on our shoulders and fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

162
00:13:09,424 --> 00:13:11,072
what are we going to be asked about?

163
00:13:11,856 --> 00:13:14,139
We had no businesses, because you see …

164
00:13:14,239 --> 00:13:16,970
لا تزول قدما عبد يوم القيامة حتى يسأل عن أربع

165
00:13:17,149 --> 00:13:18,769
You are not going to move your feet,

166
00:13:19,069 --> 00:13:22,805
your feet are not gonna move from the tracks on the Day of Judgment, until you're asked four questions;

167
00:13:23,623 --> 00:13:25,823
 About your life, about your youth.

168
00:13:26,125 --> 00:13:29,294
And then the other two questions are relating to what? Money.

169
00:13:29,898 --> 00:13:32,437
How did you make money? And how did you spend it?

170
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:37,001
So two questions relate to money, and that's what's going to hold people behind.

171
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:39,234
That's what it's gonna delay them.

172
00:13:39,837 --> 00:13:43,862
Because you're going to be asked about each and every penny that you made, and that you spent.

173
00:13:44,955 --> 00:13:47,307
So these Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) said: We didn't have any money to be asked about.

174
00:13:48,264 --> 00:13:50,504
We're carrying our swords…

175
00:13:50,604 --> 00:13:53,256
على عواتقنا حدنا وحدنا في سبيل الله

176
00:13:53,297 --> 00:13:56,020
We died for the sake of Allah. So what are we going to be asked about?

177
00:13:56,518 --> 00:13:59,067
So the angel will tell them: You're welcome, come in!

178
00:14:00,038 --> 00:14:02,018
- while everybody else is still going to the Hisab(حساب).

179
00:14:02,377 --> 00:14:06,810
4) Number four: Love of your children and caring for them:

180
00:14:07,524 --> 00:14:08,923
 Is it because you care for them?

181
00:14:10,547 --> 00:14:12,770
Well, Allah is more careful for them than you.

182
00:14:13,257 --> 00:14:16,793
Didn’t He care for them while they were in the darkness of their mother's womb?

183
00:14:17,592 --> 00:14:23,169
How can such a child prevent you from Jihad(جهاد), when if he is young, you are concerned.

184
00:14:23,868 --> 00:14:26,197
And when they grow old, you are still concerned.

185
00:14:26,882 --> 00:14:31,364
You are concerned about them when they are healthy, and you're concerned about them when they're sick.

186
00:14:31,764 --> 00:14:34,187
If you discipline them, they revolt against you.

187
00:14:34,687 --> 00:14:36,437
If you advise them, they hate you.

188
00:14:37,317 --> 00:14:41,708
And after all of your care for them, when you grow old, they forsake you,

189
00:14:42,032 --> 00:14:43,503
 and you still see them as a blessing.

190
00:14:45,189 --> 00:14:50,013
Get them out of your mind and hand them over to the One, Who created them.

191
00:14:51,065 --> 00:14:55,001
And trust Allah in their provisions as He trust them in yours.

192
00:14:55,459 --> 00:15:01,069
How can you acknowledge that Allah is the One, Who manages the affairs of the heavens and earth,

193
00:15:01,448 --> 00:15:03,994
and you don't trust him with the provisions of your children?

194
00:15:04,951 --> 00:15:08,777
I mean, don't we all acknowledge that Allah is the One, Who is running the affairs of the universe?

195
00:15:09,911 --> 00:15:13,069
Don't we believe that Allah is the One, Who is providing the Rizq(رزق)

196
00:15:13,169 --> 00:15:16,943
for every fish in the sea and every animal on the land and every bird in the air?

197
00:15:17,567 --> 00:15:25,534
Don’t we believe that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is the One, Who has created and is sustaining the universe,

198
00:15:25,634 --> 00:15:27,247
this huge universe?

199
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:32,174
And then we don’t trust Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ with the provisions of our children.

200
00:15:33,409 --> 00:15:40,503
In the name of Allah, you have no authority over the harm or benefit that befalls them, or even yourself.

201
00:15:41,617 --> 00:15:45,075
You have no control even over your own life or theirs.

202
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:47,818
You cannot even add a day to their life.

203
00:15:48,919 --> 00:15:53,579
One day you would be dead and then you would leave your children, orphans behind you.

204
00:15:54,032 --> 00:15:57,847
Then you would say: I wish I were with the martyrs,

205
00:15:58,413 --> 00:16:03,306
and the response would be, now it's too late. Allah says:

206
00:16:03,805 --> 00:16:13,599
يا أَيُّهَا النّاسُ اتَّقوا رَبَّكُم وَاخشَوا يَومًا لا يَجزي والِدٌ عَن وَلَدِهِ

207
00:16:13,902 --> 00:16:20,163
وَلا مَولودٌ هُوَ جازٍ عَن والِدِهِ شَيئًا ۚ

208
00:16:20,574 --> 00:16:23,717
إِنَّ وَعدَ اللَّهِ حَقٌّ ۖ

209
00:16:24,051 --> 00:16:33,154
فَلا تَغُرَّنَّكُمُ الحَياةُ الدُّنيا وَلا يَغُرَّنَّكُم بِاللَّهِ الغَرورُ۞

210
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:39,057
Oh mankind! Fear your Lord, and fear a day when no father will avail his son,

211
00:16:39,561 --> 00:16:41,878
nor will a son avail his father at all.

212
00:16:42,745 --> 00:16:44,663
Indeed the promise of Allah is true,

213
00:16:45,158 --> 00:16:47,379
 so let not the worldly life delude you,

214
00:16:47,856 --> 00:16:51,310
and be not deceived about Allah by the deceiver, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

215
00:16:52,083 --> 00:16:54,145
And this is Luqman(لُقمان) verse 33.

216
00:16:55,022 --> 00:16:58,196
Now if your child is among the successful people of paradise,

217
00:16:59,362 --> 00:17:03,136
then you will be reunited with them in Jannah(جنة)

218
00:17:04,376 --> 00:17:06,587
and if he is among the losers, then why wait?

219
00:17:07,025 --> 00:17:08,717
Let the separation be from now.

220
00:17:10,153 --> 00:17:13,301
If you truly care for your child, then die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد),

221
00:17:13,586 --> 00:17:17,288
you would  then be able to appeal for 70 of your family-members.

222
00:17:17,588 --> 00:17:18,795
So what are you waiting for?

223
00:17:20,835 --> 00:17:26,607
Now Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز), when he was in Sakarat-Ul-Maut(سكرات الموت), when he was dying,

224
00:17:27,923 --> 00:17:31,995
Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) made things strict on his family, very strict.

225
00:17:32,893 --> 00:17:37,835
So when he was dying, his relatives, you know Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة) they are all living a very high class life,

226
00:17:38,819 --> 00:17:43,467
and now the Khalifah(خليفه) and his wife and children are living this difficult life.

227
00:17:43,567 --> 00:17:45,890
You know it's like they didn't belong to the family.

228
00:17:47,231 --> 00:17:53,181
Fatima Bint Abdul Malik(فاطمه بنت عبدالملك), the wife of Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز), was brought up in a house of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

229
00:17:53,811 --> 00:17:56,194
Her father was a Khalifah(خليفه), Abdul Malik Bin Marwan(عبدالملك بن مروان ),

230
00:17:56,879 --> 00:17:58,676
three of her brothers were Khulafa(خلفاء),

231
00:17:59,076 --> 00:18:02,015
Suleiman Bin Abdul Malik(سليمان بن عبدالملك), Hisham Bin Abdul Malik(هشام بن عبدالملك) and Waleed bin Abdul Malik(وليدبن عبدالملك),

232
00:18:02,465 --> 00:18:06,317
and she's a wife of a Khalifah(خليفه), Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) surrounded by Khulafa(خلفاء) from all over.

233
00:18:06,879 --> 00:18:10,612
Nevertheless, he took all of her jewelry and he gave it out to Sadaqah(صدقة)

234
00:18:10,876 --> 00:18:13,892
and he would have her wear very simple clothes.

235
00:18:14,963 --> 00:18:19,860
So Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة) were, putting pressure on the Khalifah(خليفه). Why are you doing this?

236
00:18:21,623 --> 00:18:25,270
So they came to him. And obviously they knew that he's not going to change his ways.

237
00:18:25,470 --> 00:18:29,516
So when he was dying, they came to him to at least convince him to do something for his kids.

238
00:18:31,395 --> 00:18:37,065
So they told him: You don't have anything to leave behind for your children, nothing.

239
00:18:38,135 --> 00:18:39,575
At least give them something.

240
00:18:40,075 --> 00:18:42,122
And it's Halal(حلال), you don't have to steal anything,

241
00:18:42,274 --> 00:18:45,570
give them like you're giving the rest of the Ummah(امة), I mean there is so much wealth in the Ummah(امة).

242
00:18:45,922 --> 00:18:49,269
They're pay every Muslim a salary for no work.

243
00:18:49,769 --> 00:18:53,214
Everybody was receiving a salary because there was so much to hand out.

244
00:18:54,494 --> 00:18:57,839
So they're telling him, he needs something for his children.

245
00:18:57,939 --> 00:19:00,169
Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) said: Bring them, bring my children.

246
00:19:00,736 --> 00:19:04,784
So they brought them and they were all lined up in front of him, all of them.

247
00:19:04,984 --> 00:19:07,161
And you know before death, it's a very difficult time,

248
00:19:07,261 --> 00:19:12,435
you know, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) can come to you and make you feel sorry for them.

249
00:19:13,687 --> 00:19:17,175
So they were all lined up in front of him wearing very simple clothes.

250
00:19:18,663 --> 00:19:24,807
And then he looked at them and he said: My son is either is a Mo'min(مؤمن) or Fajir(فاجر),

251
00:19:26,170 --> 00:19:31,219
 my children are either going to be a Mo'min(مؤمن) or a corrupt person.

252
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:40,292
He said: If they are a Mo'min(مؤمن), believers, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is going to give them Rizq(رزق),

253
00:19:41,602 --> 00:19:46,778
and if my son grows up to become corrupt, I don't want to support him in his corruption.

254
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:53,403
And he decided not to leave them anything behind, and he died without leaving them anything.

255
00:19:54,203 --> 00:19:56,304
The narrator of the story said:

256
00:19:57,210 --> 00:20:01,721
I've  later on seen the sons of Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) when they grew old.

257
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:07,937
Every one of them was a millionaire. And every one of them was Salih(صالح), everyone was righteous.

258
00:20:09,479 --> 00:20:14,663
Put your trust in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, it is better for you than what you think is right.

259
00:20:15,821 --> 00:20:17,328
فوضع امورك الى الله

260
00:20:17,893 --> 00:20:22,412
Put your affairs in the hands of Allah and let Him manage your affairs for you.

261
00:20:23,171 --> 00:20:24,539
Rasool Allah ﷺ used to say in the Dua(دُعَا),

262
00:20:24,617 --> 00:20:27,166
اللهم لا تكلني الى نفسي طرفة عين

263
00:20:27,831 --> 00:20:32,026
 O Allah don't put my affairs in my hands even if even a blink of an eye,

264
00:20:32,756 --> 00:20:36,715
even for as long as a blink of an eye, keep my affairs in your hands.

265
00:20:38,105 --> 00:20:43,829
5) Your friends, Number 5): If you are unable to leave behind your friends and acquaintances,

266
00:20:44,682 --> 00:20:46,274
then remember the day of judgment.

267
00:20:46,534 --> 00:20:52,103
On that day friends are enemies, except the righteous among them,

268
00:20:53,973 --> 00:20:58,759
so if your friends are not righteous then we don't want to be with them today.

269
00:20:58,919 --> 00:21:00,879
Because tomorrow they will turn against you.

270
00:21:02,023 --> 00:21:06,627
But if they are righteous, then Allah will unite you together in a better place, than this.

271
00:21:07,175 --> 00:21:08,655
Allah سبحانه تعالى says:

272
00:21:09,038 --> 00:21:18,983
وَنَزَعنا ما في صُدورِهِم مِن غِلٍّ إِخوانًا عَلىٰ سُرُرٍ مُتَقابِلينَ۞

273
00:21:19,336 --> 00:21:23,278
And we will remove whatever is in their breasts of resentment.

274
00:21:23,727 --> 00:21:26,986
So they will be brothers on thrones facing each other.

275
00:21:27,553 --> 00:21:32,570
وَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِى صُدُورِهِم مِّنْ غِلٍّ إِخْوَٰنًا عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍ مُّتَقَٰابِلِينَ۞

276
00:21:33,082 --> 00:21:34,783
And this is Al Hijr(ألحجر) verse 47

277
00:21:36,368 --> 00:21:38,864
6) Power and prestige:

278
00:21:39,524 --> 00:21:41,939
You might be staying behind the ranks of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين)

279
00:21:42,871 --> 00:21:50,823
because you fear the loss of what you have established so far in your life in terms of position, power, and prestige.

280
00:21:52,250 --> 00:21:57,127
This position you're holding, how many hands did it passed through until it reached you?

281
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:02,627
So if this position left them, it would one day leave you.

282
00:22:04,643 --> 00:22:09,067
Your power is temporary, and your prestige will soon be forgotten.

283
00:22:09,974 --> 00:22:14,281
Your position, power and prestige are keeping you away from the path of paradise.

284
00:22:15,483 --> 00:22:20,290
Now the lowest person in paradise will own 10 times the whole world  and everything in it.

285
00:22:21,804 --> 00:22:26,589
This is the power and position of the lowest person in paradise.

286
00:22:26,889 --> 00:22:30,494
It’s the greater than that of the greatest king of this world.

287
00:22:31,426 --> 00:22:34,375
Nothing in this world is the free of contamination.

288
00:22:35,204 --> 00:22:39,124
The position you are holding has its fair share of disappointments.

289
00:22:39,906 --> 00:22:43,305
In order to win power and positions you will have to struggle,

290
00:22:43,836 --> 00:22:46,116
you will win enemies and lose friends.

291
00:22:46,469 --> 00:22:48,744
You will suffer pain and defeats along the way.

292
00:22:49,318 --> 00:22:53,267
Paradise is free all of that, Allah says:

293
00:22:54,406 --> 00:23:05,460
جَنّاتُ عَدنٍ يَدخُلونَها وَمَن صَلَحَ مِن آبائِهِم وَأَزواجِهِم وَذُرِّيّاتِهِم ۖ

294
00:23:05,909 --> 00:23:12,565
وَالمَلائِكَةُ يَدخُلونَ عَلَيهِم مِن كُلِّ بابٍ۞

295
00:23:12,965 --> 00:23:19,091
سَلامٌ عَلَيكُم بِما صَبَرتُم ۚ فَنِعمَ عُقبَى الدّارِ۞

296
00:23:19,430 --> 00:23:22,115
Gardens of  perpetual residence,

297
00:23:22,674 --> 00:23:28,565
they will enter them with whoever were righteous among their fathers, their spouses and their descendants.

298
00:23:29,131 --> 00:23:32,564
And the angels will enter upon them from every gate saying:

299
00:23:33,007 --> 00:23:36,518
Peace be upon you for what you patiently endure.

300
00:23:37,104 --> 00:23:39,085
And excellent is the final home.

301
00:23:39,706 --> 00:23:41,649
Al-Ra'ad(ألرَّعد) Twenty three and Twenty four(23-24).

302
00:23:42,822 --> 00:23:47,261
Now, he talks about the contamination of this world.

303
00:23:49,281 --> 00:23:52,684
Jannah(جنة) is different than Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) in four areas:

304
00:23:53,170 --> 00:23:53,997
Number 1)

305
00:23:56,946 --> 00:23:58,954
الدنيا فانية والجنة باقية

306
00:23:59,781 --> 00:24:03,975
This world is temporary and Akhirah(آخرة) is permanent.

307
00:24:04,187 --> 00:24:05,473
Allah says about Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

308
00:24:05,991 --> 00:24:06,971
متاع الغرور

309
00:24:08,050 --> 00:24:09,115
And Allah says about Jannah(جنة),

310
00:24:09,175 --> 00:24:11,417
والاخرة خير وابقى

311
00:24:11,888 --> 00:24:14,154
Akhirah(آخرة) is better and everlasting.

312
00:24:15,205 --> 00:24:20,423
Number 2) There's a difference in quantity.

313
00:24:22,352 --> 00:24:25,409
Number 3) There is a difference in quality.

314
00:24:26,450 --> 00:24:30,681
Number 4) Everything in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is contaminated.

315
00:24:31,129 --> 00:24:32,916
And everything in Akhirah(آخرة) is pure.

316
00:24:33,655 --> 00:24:37,092
Number 1) Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is temporary and Akhirah(آخرة) is permanent.

317
00:24:37,868 --> 00:24:39,196
How long are you going to live in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)?

318
00:24:40,150 --> 00:24:45,675
I was watching in Al-Jazeera(ألجزيرة) and in the news strip it said that the oldest man in the world has passed away

319
00:24:46,262 --> 00:24:52,732
 in Japan at the age of 114, that's the oldest, 114.

320
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:59,066
How long will you live in Akhirah(آخرة)? Infinity.

321
00:25:01,647 --> 00:25:05,311
Now if we want to make a ratio Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) to Akhirah(آخرة).

322
00:25:07,521 --> 00:25:08,928
What do you do to make a ratio?

323
00:25:09,228 --> 00:25:11,328
You divide Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) on Akhirah(آخرة).

324
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:15,754
So 114 divided by infinity, what's the answer?

325
00:25:18,465 --> 00:25:23,911
Yani(يعني) Math tells us that it's zero. Nothing!

326
00:25:24,269 --> 00:25:25,840
There isn't even a ratio.

327
00:25:27,623 --> 00:25:32,439
But Rasool Allah ﷺ was more generous than that. He said: If this world was worth a wing of a mosquito,

328
00:25:33,900 --> 00:25:37,880
but then you can notice that Rasool Allah ﷺ said: One wing so the mosquito can't even fly.

329
00:25:38,977 --> 00:25:40,334
He didn't even say two wings.

330
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:43,153
So Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is nothing. Worthless !

331
00:25:45,117 --> 00:25:47,386
Number two. Quantity.

332
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:53,225
Musa عليه السّلام asked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, what's the lowest level in Jannah(جنة)

333
00:25:55,383 --> 00:25:56,609
and this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim(مسلم).

334
00:25:56,661 --> 00:26:01,078
There's another Hadith(حديث). Rasool Allah ﷺ talks about the lowest level in Jannah(جنة), they're quite similar.

335
00:26:03,475 --> 00:26:10,677
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The last man to come out of Hellfire, he will come out of hellfire,

336
00:26:11,524 --> 00:26:16,628
and just because he came out of Hellfire, he’s not in Jannah(جنة) yet, he is so happy.

337
00:26:17,616 --> 00:26:21,573
He will say: Oh Allah, You have given me something that you have not given to any of Your creation.

338
00:26:22,019 --> 00:26:26,438
He doesn’t what is going on in Jannah(جنة)? He just thinks that being out from hellfire is good enough,

339
00:26:27,089 --> 00:26:28,677
not good enough, he thinks that is the best.

340
00:26:29,384 --> 00:26:31,416
But then he see a tree in the horizon.

341
00:26:31,616 --> 00:26:37,104
Now this is the desolate land between Jahannum(جَهَّنَّم) and Jannah(جنة).

342
00:26:37,943 --> 00:26:39,390
So he see a tree in the horizon.

343
00:26:41,702 --> 00:26:46,386
So he says: O Allah, can You allow me to please go under that tree,

344
00:26:46,745 --> 00:26:51,889
so that I can drink from the water and eat from its fruits and enjoy its shade.

345
00:26:53,953 --> 00:26:56,381
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells him, You can go!

346
00:26:57,637 --> 00:26:58,704
So he goes under the tree.

347
00:27:00,708 --> 00:27:04,558
But then, when he get there he sees another tree.

348
00:27:09,711 --> 00:27:13,305
Now he has already told Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ before that I am not going to ask for anything more.

349
00:27:13,451 --> 00:27:18,206
He said: that’s all what I want! Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells him: Didn’t you promise that you don’t ask for anything else.

350
00:27:18,425 --> 00:27:19,984
Because he said: I want to go next to that tree.

351
00:27:21,352 --> 00:27:23,708
Allah told him: You promise that you're not going to ask for anything else.

352
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:25,599
He said: O Allah this is the last time,

353
00:27:26,404 --> 00:27:28,420
I promise, I am not ask for anything more.

354
00:27:29,349 --> 00:27:33,368
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells him: You can go. He gets there, and he sees a better tree.

355
00:27:34,316 --> 00:27:39,517
He says: O Allah, Let me go under that tree, so that I can drink from its water and eats its fruit, Allah will tell him:

356
00:27:39,817 --> 00:27:43,109
Son of Adam(آدم), didn’t you promise that you’re not going ask for anything more?

357
00:27:43,409 --> 00:27:44,317
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

358
00:27:44,348 --> 00:27:46,085
وهو لأنه يرى ما لا صبرله عليه

359
00:27:47,067 --> 00:27:49,689
The man is seeing something, and he has no patience,

360
00:27:50,262 --> 00:27:51,247
he cannot hold back.

361
00:27:52,667 --> 00:27:54,876
So he keeps on breaking his promise again and again.

362
00:27:55,194 --> 00:27:58,073
The third time Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells him: You promise!

363
00:27:58,533 --> 00:27:59,845
You are not going to ask for anything else.

364
00:27:59,889 --> 00:28:01,962
He said: I promise this is the last time.

365
00:28:02,820 --> 00:28:07,722
So he goes under another tree but then when gets under that the tree what does he see.

366
00:28:08,366 --> 00:28:09,891
He sees the walls of Jannah(جنة).

367
00:28:11,266 --> 00:28:16,579
He says: O Allah, I don’t want to go in. Just let me sit under that wall, just sit under that wall.

368
00:28:16,856 --> 00:28:22,672
And you see the thing is, because it is getting closer to Jannah(جنة), even though he's not Jannah(جنة) yet,

