551
00:43:55,882 --> 00:44:01,193
But Allah has preferred the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) over those who remain behind with a great reward.

552
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:03,299
Al-Nisa(ألنساء) Verse 95.

553
00:44:04,565 --> 00:44:06,705
In fact there's nothing that compares to Jihad(جهاد),

554
00:44:07,174 --> 00:44:12,121
the Messenger of Allah says: Standing in the ranks of the army in the battlefield

555
00:44:12,521 --> 00:44:16,349
is greater than worshiping Allah among your family for 70 years.

556
00:44:16,849 --> 00:44:18,785
That's in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Bayhaqi(بيهقي) and Al-Hakim(ألحاكم).

557
00:44:18,930 --> 00:44:21,284
Oh you, who have deceived yourself

558
00:44:21,784 --> 00:44:25,751
realize that the sleep of the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is better than the praying of the night,

559
00:44:26,063 --> 00:44:28,483
and the fasting of the day for everyone else.

560
00:44:28,883 --> 00:44:30,738
Number 9). Love of your wife.

561
00:44:31,409 --> 00:44:35,744
Tayeb(طيِّب), If you cannot go to Jihad(جهاد) because you are attached to a beautiful wife,

562
00:44:37,466 --> 00:44:42,338
then even if you were to assume that your wife is the best woman in the whole world,

563
00:44:43,325 --> 00:44:46,311
and that she is the most beautiful woman in the whole world.

564
00:44:47,312 --> 00:44:54,033
Now didn't she start out as a lowly droplet and would end as a decomposed body.

565
00:44:54,949 --> 00:45:00,177
And in between her birth and death, she never ceased carrying stool in her gut,

566
00:45:01,657 --> 00:45:06,009
her menstrual period keeps you away from her for a good portion of her life,

567
00:45:06,953 --> 00:45:09,749
her disobedience is more than her obedience.

568
00:45:10,357 --> 00:45:13,534
If she does not wash, she would smell horrible.

569
00:45:13,934 --> 00:45:16,805
If she doesn't comb, her hair becomes ruffled,

570
00:45:17,251 --> 00:45:19,840
the older she gets the more ugly she becomes,

571
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:22,221
pleasing her is not easy.

572
00:45:26,196 --> 00:45:28,049
And her love costs you a lot.

573
00:45:29,342 --> 00:45:33,688
You're always trying to impress her. And nothing is ever enough.

574
00:45:34,707 --> 00:45:37,598
She only loves you, when you give her what she wants.

575
00:45:38,218 --> 00:45:41,444
And if you don't she would soon leave you and find someone else.

576
00:45:42,381 --> 00:45:45,584
As if she's telling you, if you want me spend on me.

577
00:45:46,307 --> 00:45:50,298
In general, you cannot enjoy her without enduring pain and suffering.

578
00:45:51,523 --> 00:45:55,551
It is amazing how such a woman is keeping you away from the woman of paradise.

579
00:45:56,051 --> 00:46:02,493
In the Name of Allah, the blood of the Shaheed(شَهِيد), does not dry before he meets his wife in paradise.

580
00:46:03,765 --> 00:46:10,069
She is beautiful with big lustrous eyes, a virgin, as if she is an emerald.

581
00:46:10,769 --> 00:46:13,883
She has loved no one, and will love, no one but you.

582
00:46:14,811 --> 00:46:17,238
She was created for you and only you.

583
00:46:18,276 --> 00:46:20,757
If her finger appears it would overshadow the moon.

584
00:46:21,468 --> 00:46:26,390
If her bracelet appears in the dark night, it will leave no darkness in the universe.

585
00:46:27,451 --> 00:46:32,331
If her wrist appears, it would take away the mind of every sane human being,

586
00:46:33,368 --> 00:46:39,304
if she appears between the heaven and earth, the distance between them would be filled by her scent.

587
00:46:39,729 --> 00:46:44,549
And if she splits in the oceans of the world, the salt water would turn fresh.

588
00:46:45,464 --> 00:46:48,401
The more you look at her, the more beautiful, she becomes,

589
00:46:48,746 --> 00:46:51,703
the more time you spend with her, the more you love her,

590
00:46:51,903 --> 00:46:56,174
doesn't make any sense to learn about such a woman, and not try to meet her.

591
00:46:57,064 --> 00:47:01,150
What about when you learn that you will not be married to one but 70 of the Hoor(حور).

592
00:47:02,049 --> 00:47:05,201
Keep in mind that leaving your wife behind is inevitable.

593
00:47:05,711 --> 00:47:12,186
You will die and so would she and In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله) you will be reunited in paradise.

594
00:47:12,586 --> 00:47:15,804
And then you will find her to be even more beautiful than the Hoor(حور).

595
00:47:16,904 --> 00:47:22,507
When that happens you will find her free of all of the contaminations of this worldly life,

596
00:47:23,372 --> 00:47:24,835
wake up before it's too late.

597
00:47:25,439 --> 00:47:31,004
Free yourself from the prison of this world, and pray to Allah to grant your martyrdom.

598
00:47:31,404 --> 00:47:35,001
Don't let anything stand between you and this great reward.

599
00:47:35,751 --> 00:47:39,616
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrates that the messenger of Allah said: The Shaheed(شَهِيد) feels the pain of death,

600
00:47:40,116 --> 00:47:43,397
 just like one of you would feel the sting of an insect.

601
00:47:44,063 --> 00:47:45,563
And this Hadith(حديث) is Hasan(حسن),

602
00:47:46,084 --> 00:47:48,798
it is narrated At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Nisai(نسائ), Ibn Majah(إبن ماجه) and Ahmad(أحمد).

603
00:47:50,908 --> 00:47:52,565
So this is the end of Mo'adha(مؤعظه)

604
00:47:55,167 --> 00:47:58,043
The of the virtues of Jihad(جهاد). Allah سبحانه تعالى says:

605
00:47:58,590 --> 00:48:11,842
لا يَستَوِي القاعِدونَ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ غَيرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ وَالمُجاهِدونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم ۚ

606
00:48:12,589 --> 00:48:21,428
فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ المُجاهِدينَ بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم عَلَى القاعِدينَ دَرَجَةً ۚ

607
00:48:21,959 --> 00:48:26,311
وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الحُسنىٰ ۚ

608
00:48:26,511 --> 00:48:33,458
وَفَضَّلَ اللَّهُ المُجاهِدينَ عَلَى القاعِدينَ أَجرًا عَظيمًا۞

609
00:48:34,044 --> 00:48:43,597
دَرَجاتٍ مِنهُ وَمَغفِرَةً وَرَحمَةً ۚ وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفورًا رَحيمًا۞

610
00:48:43,923 --> 00:48:49,367
Not equal are those believers remaining at home, Other than the disabled,

611
00:48:49,836 --> 00:48:54,050
and the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) in the cause of Allah with their wealth and their lives.

612
00:48:55,512 --> 00:48:58,459
Allah has preferred the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) through their wealth and their lives

613
00:48:58,559 --> 00:49:01,376
over those who remain behind by degrees.

614
00:49:01,754 --> 00:49:05,020
And to all, Allah has promised the best reward.

615
00:49:05,570 --> 00:49:09,817
But Allah has preferred the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) over those who remained behind with a great reward,

616
00:49:10,311 --> 00:49:12,783
degrees for him and forgiveness and mercy.

617
00:49:13,098 --> 00:49:17,098
And Allah is Ever forgiving and merciful. An-Nisa(أنساء) Verse 95-96.

618
00:49:17,198 --> 00:49:21,111
Now in this Ayah(آية) two things can be derived from it.

619
00:49:22,591 --> 00:49:26,876
First of all, Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب) is Fardh Kifayah(فرض كفاية) and its not Fardh Ain(فرض عين).

620
00:49:28,342 --> 00:49:31,256
That the offensive Jihad(جهاد) is Fardh Kifayah(فرض كفاية).

621
00:49:32,403 --> 00:49:36,959
Because we mentioned that Saeed bin Musaib(سعيد بن مسيب) holds the view

622
00:49:37,672 --> 00:49:40,210
that Jihad(جهاد) is Fardh Ain(فرض عين), we are talking about Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب).

623
00:49:41,422 --> 00:49:47,306
But this Ayah(آية) is comparing between the two, and is saying that to all that Allah has promise reward.

624
00:49:48,270 --> 00:49:51,701
So how can Allah say that is He is promising a reward, when somebody is doing a sin.

625
00:49:52,763 --> 00:49:55,876
So this is an evidence that Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب), the offensive Jihad(جهاد) is Fardh Kifayah(فرض كفاية),

626
00:49:57,450 --> 00:50:01,058
but it's also an evidence that Jihad(جهاد) is the best of deeds

627
00:50:02,525 --> 00:50:04,644
that there there's nothing better than the Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

628
00:50:05,430 --> 00:50:08,096
because Allah explicitly states

629
00:50:08,596 --> 00:50:10,697
that the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) are better than the Qaai’din(قاعدين)

630
00:50:10,797 --> 00:50:12,996
and the Qaai’din(قاعدين) is talking about the Qaai’din(قاعدين) in general,

631
00:50:13,929 --> 00:50:17,047
whether they are bad, whether they are scholars,

632
00:50:17,549 --> 00:50:20,248
whether they are serving in the house of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

633
00:50:20,704 --> 00:50:22,709
Whether they are giving Sadaqat(صدقات).

634
00:50:23,728 --> 00:50:28,680
Al-Qaai’din(ألقاعدين) in general, no matter what they do, are lower in status than the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

635
00:50:32,813 --> 00:50:33,713
Allah says:

636
00:50:34,721 --> 00:50:43,078
فَليُقاتِل في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذينَ يَشرونَ الحَياةَ الدُّنيا بِالآخِرَةِ ۚ

637
00:50:43,500 --> 00:50:53,483
وَمَن يُقاتِل في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَيُقتَل أَو يَغلِب فَسَوفَ نُؤتيهِ أَجرًا عَظيمًا۞

638
00:50:53,908 --> 00:50:59,477
So let those fight in the cause of Allah, who sells the life of this world for the hereafter.

639
00:51:00,135 --> 00:51:04,710
And he who fight in the cause of a Allah and is killed or achieves victory.

640
00:51:05,126 --> 00:51:07,633
We will bestow upon him a great reward,

641
00:51:08,133 --> 00:51:09,613
An-Nisa(أنساء) Verse 74.

642
00:51:09,999 --> 00:51:18,011
الَّذينَ آمَنوا وَهاجَروا وَجاهَدوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَموالِهِم

643
00:51:18,465 --> 00:51:25,875
بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم أَعظَمُ دَرَجَةً عِندَ اللَّهِ ۚ

644
00:51:25,975 --> 00:51:33,853
وَأُولٰئِكَ هُمُ الفائِزونَ ۞

645
00:51:33,971 --> 00:51:46,841
 يُبَشِّرُهُم رَبُّهُم بِرَحمَةٍ مِنهُ وَرِضوانٍ وَجَنّاتٍ لَهُم فيها نَعيمٌ مُقيمٌ ۞

646
00:51:47,524 --> 00:51:52,679
خالِدينَ فيها أَبَدًا ۚ

647
00:51:53,079 --> 00:51:59,368
إِنَّ اللَّهَ عِندَهُ أَجرٌ عَظيمٌ۞

648
00:52:00,224 --> 00:52:08,424
The ones, who have believed, emigrated and striven in the cause of Allah with their wealth and their lives,

649
00:52:08,770 --> 00:52:11,238
are greater in rank in the sight of Allah.

650
00:52:12,005 --> 00:52:17,301
And it is those who are the attainers, of success.

651
00:52:17,954 --> 00:52:21,247
Their Lord gives them good tidings of mercy from Him

652
00:52:21,747 --> 00:52:25,995
and approval, and of gardens for them wherein is enduring pleasure,

653
00:52:26,434 --> 00:52:30,147
abiding therein forever indeed, Allah has with him a great reward,

654
00:52:30,247 --> 00:52:31,735
At-Taubah(ألتوبة) Verse 20-22.

655
00:52:32,616 --> 00:52:34,083
In At-Taubah(ألتوبة) Verse 111,

656
00:52:34,663 --> 00:52:42,481
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشتَرىٰ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ أَنفُسَهُم وَأَموالَهُم

657
00:52:42,681 --> 00:52:47,641
 وَأَموالَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الجَنَّةَ ۚ

658
00:52:47,941 --> 00:52:55,031
يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَيَقتُلونَ وَيُقتَلونَ ۖ

659
00:52:55,331 --> 00:53:03,549
وَعدًا عَلَيهِ حَقًّا فِي التَّوراةِ وَالإِنجيلِ وَالقُرآنِ ۚ

660
00:53:03,749 --> 00:53:08,063
وَمَن أَوفىٰ بِعَهدِهِ مِنَ اللَّهِ ۚ

661
00:53:08,396 --> 00:53:13,875
فَاستَبشِروا بِبَيعِكُمُ الَّذي بايَعتُم بِهِ ۚ

662
00:53:14,175 --> 00:53:18,603
وَذٰلِكَ هُوَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ۞

663
00:53:18,939 --> 00:53:24,239
Indeed, Allah has purchased from the believers their lives and their properties

664
00:53:24,279 --> 00:53:27,475
in exchange for that, they will have paradise.

665
00:53:28,136 --> 00:53:31,576
They fight in the cause of Allah, so they kill and are killed.

666
00:53:33,198 --> 00:53:39,395
It is a true promise binding upon him in the Torah(توراة) and the Gospel and the Qur'an,

667
00:53:39,828 --> 00:53:42,382
and who is truer to his covenant than Allah.

668
00:53:42,849 --> 00:53:46,373
So rejoice in your transaction, which you have contracted,

669
00:53:46,673 --> 00:53:48,909
and it is that which is the great attainment.

670
00:53:49,182 --> 00:53:51,727
Two things in this Ayah(آية). Number one,

671
00:53:52,567 --> 00:53:53,697
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشْتَرَىٰ

672
00:53:54,555 --> 00:53:56,848
Allah has bought.

673
00:53:58,434 --> 00:54:07,636
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is offering you to buy your soul and your wealth,

674
00:54:08,536 --> 00:54:10,577
Allah wants to buy something from you.

675
00:54:11,828 --> 00:54:12,959
And that is your soul.

676
00:54:14,578 --> 00:54:18,057
And Allah is offering you as one of the scholars said,

677
00:54:18,879 --> 00:54:21,189
أشتارى منهم وأغلالهم سَمن

678
00:54:22,102 --> 00:54:28,888
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ offered to buy from them, and he set a very, very high price.

679
00:54:31,840 --> 00:54:37,251
Allah, is going to pay for the price of your soul, Jannah(جنة).

680
00:54:39,205 --> 00:54:41,164
The most expensive commodity.

681
00:54:42,748 --> 00:54:46,434
When the Ansaar(أنصار) were meeting with Rasool Allah ﷺ in ‘Baiyat-Ul-Aqabah As-Thaniya(بيعةالعقبة ألثانية),

682
00:54:47,571 --> 00:54:52,113
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is what I want from you,

683
00:54:54,054 --> 00:54:58,230
you testify that there's no God but Allah and that I’m the Messenger of Allah,

684
00:54:59,268 --> 00:55:04,942
and you protect me from that which you protect your wives and children.

685
00:55:07,699 --> 00:55:12,094
Therefore, this was called Bai'yah-Tun-Nisa(بيعةالنساء), the pledge of woman, Why?

686
00:55:12,541 --> 00:55:19,277
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking for the protection that the Ansaar(أنصار) would give to their woman and property.

687
00:55:23,964 --> 00:55:26,216
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, this is what I want from you.

688
00:55:27,650 --> 00:55:34,220
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(رواحة) said: That is what you're asking from us, what will we get in exchange.

689
00:55:34,656 --> 00:55:37,031
I mean this is a deal here, we're negotiating a deal.

690
00:55:38,000 --> 00:55:40,614
This is what you want from us, what are you going to pay us back.

691
00:55:42,189 --> 00:55:45,648
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not tell them you're going to become wealthy.

692
00:55:46,590 --> 00:55:50,155
He didn't say, I'm going to appoint you as ministers in my government.

693
00:55:51,240 --> 00:55:54,259
He didn't tell them, you're going to become kings after I pass away.

694
00:55:55,238 --> 00:55:56,618
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them,

695
00:55:56,914 --> 00:55:58,054
لَكُم الجنة

696
00:55:58,838 --> 00:55:59,977
 You will get Jannah(جنة).!

697
00:56:00,584 --> 00:56:01,774
What did the Ansaar(أنصار), says:

698
00:56:01,898 --> 00:56:05,218
قَالُوا: رَبِحَ الْبَيْعُ لَا نُقِيلُ وَلَا نَسْتَقِيلُ

699
00:56:05,651 --> 00:56:09,802
This is a very profitable deal. We will never back out of it.

700
00:56:12,087 --> 00:56:17,595
So the agreement is that you give Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ your soul or your wealth, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ in exchange will give you Jannah(جنة).

701
00:56:17,763 --> 00:56:18,870
That's number one. Number two,

702
00:56:19,689 --> 00:56:25,461
the Ayah(آية) says that this contract is even mentioned in the Torah(توراة) and Gospel.

703
00:56:27,173 --> 00:56:35,253
You see with the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah, like Hud(هود), Saleh(صالح), Nooh(نوح)

704
00:56:36,413 --> 00:56:40,684
it wasn’t part of their Shariah(شريعة) to fight, Qital(قتال) wasn’t part of their Shariah(شريعة),

705
00:56:41,284 --> 00:56:44,529
Hood عليه السّلام and his followers were not given the instruction to fight.

706
00:56:45,550 --> 00:56:47,325
They were given the instructions to leave,

707
00:56:48,025 --> 00:56:53,190
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ through a supernatural event will destroy the enemy.

708
00:56:54,771 --> 00:56:58,160
With Saleh عليه السّلام the same thing with Nooh عليه السّلام, the flood,

709
00:56:58,528 --> 00:57:04,744
with Lut عليه السّلام, the destruction of the people of Lut(لوط),

710
00:57:05,697 --> 00:57:07,993
so they were not given the command to fight.

711
00:57:08,806 --> 00:57:12,567
This was a command reserved for the latter nations,

712
00:57:13,067 --> 00:57:17,045
and the first Ummah(امة) to fight Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) is the Ummah(امة) of who?

713
00:57:17,945 --> 00:57:18,882
Musa عليه السّلام

714
00:57:20,289 --> 00:57:26,324
and that's what makes Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل), the greatest Ummah(امة) after the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ

715
00:57:26,388 --> 00:57:28,303
because it's an Ummah(امة) of Da'wah(دعوة) and Jihad(جهاد).

716
00:57:29,744 --> 00:57:35,390
Therefore, this is something mentioned in the Tor'ah(توراة), and mentioned in an Injeel(إنجيل) and mentioned in Qur'an.

717
00:57:36,898 --> 00:57:38,034
Muhammad(محمد) Verse 7.

718
00:57:38,334 --> 00:57:50,538
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِن تَنصُرُوا اللَّهَ يَنصُركُم وَيُثَبِّت أَقدامَكُم۞

719
00:57:50,876 --> 00:57:57,344
 Oh you have believed. If you support Allah, He will support you and plant firmly your feet.

720
00:57:57,744 --> 00:57:59,133
In Al-Hujrat(ألحجرات) Verse15.

721
00:57:59,233 --> 00:58:08,063
إِنَّمَا المُؤمِنونَ الَّذينَ آمَنوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسولِهِ ثُمَّ لَم يَرتابوا

722
00:58:08,323 --> 00:58:17,091
ثُمَّ لَم يَرتابوا وَجاهَدوا بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ

723
00:58:17,391 --> 00:58:22,188
أُولٰئِكَ هُمُ الصّادِقونَ۞

724
00:58:22,450 --> 00:58:27,040
The believers are only the ones, who have believed in Allah and His messenger

725
00:58:27,140 --> 00:58:33,195
and then doubt not but strive make Jihad(جهاد) with their properties and their lives in the cause of Allah.

726
00:58:33,695 --> 00:58:35,556
It is those who are truthful.

727
00:58:37,357 --> 00:58:40,108
In As-Saff(ألصَّف), Verse 10 to 13.

728
00:58:40,574 --> 00:58:52,530
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا هَل أَدُلُّكُم عَلىٰ تِجارَةٍ تُنجيكُم مِن عَذابٍ أَليمٍ ۞

729
00:58:53,201 --> 00:59:03,112
تُؤمِنونَ بِاللَّهِ وَرَسولِهِ وَتُجاهِدونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَموالِكُم وَأَنفُسِكُم ۚ

730
00:59:03,852 --> 00:59:09,608
ذٰلِكُم خَيرٌ لَكُم إِن كُنتُم تَعلَمونَ۞

731
00:59:10,208 --> 00:59:19,584
يَغفِر لَكُم ذُنوبَكُم وَيُدخِلكُم جَنّاتٍ تَجري مِن تَحتِهَا الأَنهارُ

732
00:59:19,947 --> 00:59:25,089
وَمَساكِنَ طَيِّبَةً في جَنّاتِ عَدنٍ ۚ

733
00:59:25,255 --> 00:59:28,280
ذٰلِكَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ ۞

734
00:59:28,680 --> 00:59:35,728
وَأُخرىٰ تُحِبّونَها ۖ نَصرٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَفَتحٌ قَريبٌ ۗ

735
00:59:36,128 --> 00:59:39,019
وَبَشِّرِ المُؤمِنينَ۞

736
00:59:39,730 --> 00:59:44,428
Oh you have believed Shall I guide you to a transaction that will save you from painful punishment.

737
00:59:45,119 --> 00:59:47,396
It is that you believe in Allah and His messenger

738
00:59:47,596 --> 00:59:52,536
and strive in the cause of Allah with your wealth and your lives, that is best for you.

739
00:59:52,947 --> 00:59:54,272
If you should, but know.

740
00:59:54,626 --> 00:59:59,991
He will forgive you your sins and admit you to gardens beneath which rivers flow,

741
01:00:00,391 --> 01:00:04,103
and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence.

742
01:00:04,635 --> 01:00:06,202
That is a great attainment.

743
01:00:07,424 --> 01:00:14,611
And you will obtain another favor that you love, victory from Allah, and an eminent conquest

744
01:00:15,079 --> 01:00:17,501
and give good tidings to the believers.

745
01:00:18,069 --> 01:00:23,617
Jihad(جهاد) is the best deed after Salah(صلاة) and being dutiful towards one's parents,

746
01:00:24,435 --> 01:00:26,243
the Messenger of Allah was asked:

747
01:00:26,895 --> 01:00:30,754
What is the most beloved act of worship in the eyes of Allah.

748
01:00:31,554 --> 01:00:34,063
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Praying on time.

749
01:00:34,481 --> 01:00:35,578
I said: Then what?

750
01:00:35,921 --> 01:00:38,494
He said: Being dutiful towards your parents.

751
01:00:38,794 --> 01:00:42,329
I said: Then what? He said: Jihad(جهاد) in the path of Allah.

752
01:00:42,924 --> 01:00:44,453
This Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

753
01:00:45,802 --> 01:00:50,840
Ibn-e-Umar(إبن عمر) used to consider Jihad(جهاد) to be the best of all deeds after Salah(صلاة).

754
01:00:51,240 --> 01:00:53,010
And this is mentioned by Al-Bahaqi(ألبيهقي).

755
01:00:54,638 --> 01:00:59,365
The next heading: Jihad(جهاد) is the greatest deed, after believing in Allah.

756
01:01:00,682 --> 01:01:04,639
Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked, what is the best of all acts of worship.

757
01:01:04,970 --> 01:01:06,228
He said: Believing in Allah.

758
01:01:06,867 --> 01:01:08,307
He was then asked, and then what?

759
01:01:08,643 --> 01:01:10,573
He responded: Jihad(جهاد) in the path of Allah.

760
01:01:11,173 --> 01:01:12,488
Then he was asked, and then what?

761
01:01:12,688 --> 01:01:14,790
He said an accepted Hajj(حَجْ).

762
01:01:16,276 --> 01:01:18,287
That's in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم).

763
01:01:19,441 --> 01:01:26,174
In Musnad Imam Ahmad(مَسنداِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ), Ma'az(معز) narrates the Messenger of Allah was asked, what is the best deed.?

764
01:01:26,374 --> 01:01:33,387
He said: Believing in Allah, and then Jihad(جهاد), and then Hajj(حَجْ), which would be, better than every other deed,

765
01:01:33,687 --> 01:01:36,435
like the distance between the sunset, and the sunrise.

766
01:01:37,319 --> 01:01:42,332
So, believing in Allah, Jihad(جهاد) and Hajj(حَجْ) are way above everything else.

767
01:01:43,206 --> 01:01:48,402
These three deeds are above everything else, this is between sunrise and sunset.

768
01:01:48,902 --> 01:01:53,803
In Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) Abu Dhar(ابوذر) narrates, I asked the Messenger of Allah above the best deeds.

769
01:01:53,903 --> 01:01:57,272
He said believing in Allah and Jihad(جهاد) in His path.

770
01:01:59,473 --> 01:02:04,849
Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة) narrates that the Messenger of Allah stood and delivered a reminder to them

771
01:02:05,116 --> 01:02:10,703
and said that Jihad(جهاد) in the path of Allah, and believing in Allah are the greatest deeds.

772
01:02:12,004 --> 01:02:14,638
A man stood up and asked, Oh messenger of Allah:

773
01:02:15,045 --> 01:02:19,632
What if I was killed in the path of Allah would my sins be forgiven,

774
01:02:20,033 --> 01:02:21,740
the Messenger of Allah said: Yes!

775
01:02:22,094 --> 01:02:23,181
And this is in Muslim(مسلم).

776
01:02:25,050 --> 01:02:27,347
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrates that the Messenger of Allah said:

777
01:02:28,127 --> 01:02:33,297
The best of deeds in  eyes of Allah are, a belief in Allah with conviction,

778
01:02:33,688 --> 01:02:35,144
the Ghazoo(غزؤ) with no Ghalool(غلول).

779
01:02:36,318 --> 01:02:39,899
Ghalool(غلول) is money unlawfully taken from the Ghanimah(غنيمه),

780
01:02:40,607 --> 01:02:42,164
and an acceptable Hajj(حَجْ).

781
01:02:42,564 --> 01:02:43,462
The next heading:

782
01:02:44,851 --> 01:02:49,420
Jihad(جهاد) is greater than worshiping in the house of Allah and serving it and serving the pilgrims.

783
01:02:50,091 --> 01:02:55,860
An-Noman Ibn Bashir(نعمان إبن بشير) narrates. I was sitting next to the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah.

784
01:02:56,277 --> 01:02:57,839
When a man came and said:

785
01:02:59,731 --> 01:03:05,219
I wouldn't mind if I don't do anything after becoming a Muslim but serving the pilgrims,

786
01:03:05,570 --> 01:03:06,441
meaning after saying:

787
01:03:06,541 --> 01:03:08,623
أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُول الله

788
01:03:08,991 --> 01:03:14,845
I wouldn't mind doing nothing but serving the pilgrims, meaning I consider this to be the best of deeds.

789
01:03:16,524 --> 01:03:24,164
Another man said: I wouldn't mind if I don't do anything after becoming a Muslim but praying in the sacred Masjid(مسجد),

790
01:03:24,364 --> 01:03:25,283
in Masjid-Al-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام).

791
01:03:26,405 --> 01:03:31,597
A third man said: No! Jihad(جهاد) in the path of Allah is better than what you said.

792
01:03:32,463 --> 01:03:34,166
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) scolded them

793
01:03:34,874 --> 01:03:39,421
and told them to stay quiet and not raise their voices next to the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah.

794
01:03:40,426 --> 01:03:46,709
He then said, this is Friday, and in short while, Muhammadﷺ will come out of his house and give us Khut'ba(خطبة).

795
01:03:47,076 --> 01:03:49,368
And I'll ask him about what you said.

796
01:03:50,677 --> 01:03:55,047
He asked Muhammadﷺ and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed the Ayah(آية).

797
01:03:55,447 --> 01:04:04,264
أَجَعَلتُم سِقايَةَ الحاجِّ وَعِمارَةَ المَسجِدِ الحَرامِ كَمَن

798
01:04:04,656 --> 01:04:12,173
كَمَن آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَاليَومِ الآخِرِ وَجاهَدَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ

799
01:04:12,573 --> 01:04:16,832
لا يَستَوونَ عِندَ اللَّهِ ۗ

800
01:04:17,032 --> 01:04:21,919
وَاللَّهُ لا يَهدِي القَومَ الظّالِمينَ۞

801
01:04:23,006 --> 01:04:26,484
Have you made the providing of water for the pilgrim,

802
01:04:26,620 --> 01:04:28,750
and the maintenance of the Masjid-Al-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام),

803
01:04:29,150 --> 01:04:33,586
equal to one, who believes in Allah and the Last Day and mixed Jihad(جهاد) in His cause.

804
01:04:33,938 --> 01:04:36,332
They are not equal in the sight of Allah

805
01:04:36,991 --> 01:04:39,472
and Allah does not guide the wrong doing people.

806
01:04:39,906 --> 01:04:42,115
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim(ألمسلم).

807
01:04:42,870 --> 01:04:50,153
So this Ayah(آية), explicitly states that Jihad(جهاد) is better than serving the pilgrims in Masjid-Al-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام)

808
01:04:50,376 --> 01:04:52,296
and worshipping Allah in Masjid-Al-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام).

809
01:04:53,858 --> 01:04:56,300
Tayeb(طيِّب), References that Jihad(جهاد) is the greatest deed of all.

810
01:04:57,519 --> 01:05:03,337
Amr Bin Absa(عمروبن عبسة) narrates, a man came to the Messenger of Allah and said: What is Islam.?

811
01:05:04,826 --> 01:05:12,047
He said: Islam is submission of your heart, and that the Muslims are safe from your tongue and your hands.

812
01:05:13,668 --> 01:05:15,554
He said: What is the best of Islam?

813
01:05:16,255 --> 01:05:17,817
The Messenger of Allah said: Eeman(ايمان)!

814
01:05:18,753 --> 01:05:19,947
He said: And what is Eeman(ايمان)?

815
01:05:20,347 --> 01:05:29,400
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers and the resurrection after death.

816
01:05:30,126 --> 01:05:34,509
He said: What is the best of Eeman(ايمان)?

817
01:05:35,329 --> 01:05:37,198
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Hijrah(هجرة)!

818
01:05:37,800 --> 01:05:43,917
He said: What is Hijrah(هجرة)?

819
01:05:44,385 --> 01:05:47,181
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: To leave sins behind.

820
01:05:48,006 --> 01:05:50,017
He said: What is the best of Hijrah(هجرة)?

821
01:05:50,364 --> 01:05:52,345
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Jihad(جهاد)!

822
01:05:52,991 --> 01:05:54,830
He then said: What is the best of Jihad(جهاد)?

823
01:05:55,161 --> 01:06:00,866
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: The one, whose horse is slain, and His blood is spilled.

824
01:06:01,625 --> 01:06:03,629
And this is in Ahmad(أحمد), Tabrani(طبراني) and Bahaqi(بيهقي).

825
01:06:04,029 --> 01:06:07,843
So now again. He asked about Islam.

826
01:06:09,184 --> 01:06:12,413
He then asked what is the best of Islam? Rasool Ullah told him. Eeman(ايمان)!

827
01:06:13,803 --> 01:06:15,483
He said: Then, what is the best of the Eeman(ايمان).?

828
01:06:15,783 --> 01:06:17,253
He said: The best of Eeman(ايمان) is Hijrah(هجرة).

829
01:06:17,513 --> 01:06:18,910
What's the best of the Hijrah(هجرة)?

830
01:06:19,210 --> 01:06:20,587
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Jihad(جهاد)!

831
01:06:21,132 --> 01:06:24,495
And what's the best of Jihad(جهاد)? Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Martyrdom!

832
01:06:25,574 --> 01:06:30,390
Therefore, Jihad(جهاد) becomes the best, of the best, of the best.

833
01:06:31,315 --> 01:06:33,518
And then the best of that is martyrdom.

834
01:06:34,065 --> 01:06:36,007
So it's the cream of the cream of the cream.

835
01:06:36,576 --> 01:06:40,262
The Messenger of Allah told the man become a Muslim.

836
01:06:41,325 --> 01:06:42,753
The man said: What is Islam?

837
01:06:43,619 --> 01:06:47,544
 He responded to him and then he asked him about Hijrah(هجرة) and Jihad(جهاد),

838
01:06:48,044 --> 01:06:49,367
the man said: What is Jihad(جهاد).?

839
01:06:49,855 --> 01:06:52,349
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You fight in the cause of Allah

840
01:06:52,749 --> 01:06:54,881
and you do not fear fighting the enemy,

841
01:06:55,181 --> 01:06:57,127
and you do not commit Ghalool(غلول),

842
01:06:57,450 --> 01:06:58,717
and that is in Bayhaqi(البيهقي).

843
01:06:59,117 --> 01:07:03,815
In Bukhari(بخاريْ), Ayesha(عائشه) narrates that she told the Messenger of Allah,

844
01:07:03,915 --> 01:07:08,695
O messenger of Allah, we see that Jihad(جهاد) in the Cause of Allah is the Greatest deed.

845
01:07:09,182 --> 01:07:11,086
Shouldn't we then make Jihad(جهاد).

846
01:07:11,486 --> 01:07:18,863
So, here the Hadith(حديث) is saying that the even the women used to considered Jihad(جهاد) to be the greatest of deeds.

847
01:07:18,915 --> 01:07:22,059
I mean, it was common knowledge, that is the greatest of deeds.

848
01:07:22,425 --> 01:07:26,188
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them for you the best Jihad(جهاد) is Hajj Mabror(حج مبرور).

849
01:07:27,905 --> 01:07:30,429
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrates that the Messenger of Allah said:

850
01:07:31,301 --> 01:07:34,777
The Jihad(جهاد) of the old, the weak and the women is Hajj(حَجْ) and Umrah(عمرة).

851
01:07:36,701 --> 01:07:39,810
Al-Khateeb Al-Bagdadi(ألخطيب ألبغدادي) mentions in the history of Baghdad,

852
01:07:40,534 --> 01:07:43,394
and Ibn Asakir(إبن عساكر) mentions in the history of Damascus

853
01:07:43,994 --> 01:07:46,818
that Muhammad Ibn Fudhail Ibn Ayyadh(محمدإبن فضيل إبن عياض), said:

854
01:07:47,832 --> 01:07:50,064
I saw Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) in my dream.

855
01:07:50,671 --> 01:07:53,257
Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) and Fudhail Bin Ayyadh(فضيل بن عياض) were friends.

856
01:07:55,490 --> 01:07:59,451
But they we're following two different tracks.

857
01:08:01,020 --> 01:08:05,296
Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) was a scholar of Jihad(جهاد)

858
01:08:06,403 --> 01:08:08,791
and Al-Fuzail(ألفضيل) was a scholar of Ibadah(عبادة).

859
01:08:08,891 --> 01:08:12,823
So both of them were scholars, but one of them chose the track of Jihad(جهاد),

860
01:08:13,255 --> 01:08:15,922
and the other one chose the track of a Ibadah(عبادة).

861
01:08:16,597 --> 01:08:18,449
And there's the famous lines of poetry.

862
01:08:19,193 --> 01:08:24,005
When Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) sends a letter to his friend Fudhail Bin Ayyadh(فضيل بن عياض), and he tells him,

863
01:08:24,075 --> 01:08:29,710
يا عبدالحرمين يا أبصرتنا۞۞۞  ألعلمتا اَنَّك باالعبادة فالعبد۞۞۞

864
01:08:30,487 --> 01:08:33,039
O, the one, who was worshipping next to Al-Haram(ألحرم),

865
01:08:33,339 --> 01:08:41,507
if you see us, you would realize that your worship is nothing but playing, compared to what we are doing.

866
01:08:42,097 --> 01:08:45,563
So he saw Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) in a dream.

867
01:08:45,663 --> 01:08:46,983
Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن ألمبارك) passed away before him.

868
01:08:47,395 --> 01:08:48,400
He saw him in a dream.

869
01:08:49,485 --> 01:08:53,360
So I asked him: What did you, find your best deeds to be?

870
01:08:53,751 --> 01:09:00,570
He said: The deed that I preoccupied myself with, the deed that kept me busy.

871
01:09:00,906 --> 01:09:02,994
I asked: Jihad(جهاد) and Ribat(رباط).?

872
01:09:03,551 --> 01:09:04,497
He said: Yes!

873
01:09:04,952 --> 01:09:10,364
I told him. What did Allah do to you.? He said: He forgave me, he forgave me.

874
01:09:10,986 --> 01:09:19,599
And it's common to see dreams of Salaheen(ألصالحين) and the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء),

875
01:09:20,243 --> 01:09:21,905
and to ask him what happened to you?

876
01:09:22,005 --> 01:09:26,954
This is a dream that happens quite frequently.

877
01:09:28,088 --> 01:09:32,283
Al-Fadhal Bin Zaid(الفضل بن زيد) said: I heard about Abu Abdullah Imam Ahmed(أبوعبدالله إمام أحمد),

878
01:09:33,242 --> 01:09:34,903
when Ghazoo(غزؤ) was mentioned to him.

879
01:09:35,878 --> 01:09:38,359
So Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(إمام أحمد بن حنبل) was sitting in a Halaqah(حلقه) and

880
01:09:38,659 --> 01:09:41,564
the issue of Jihad(جهاد) was brought up so Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) started to cry.

881
01:09:42,264 --> 01:09:45,474
And then he said: There is no act of worship greater than it,

882
01:09:46,473 --> 01:09:49,242
there is nothing greater than Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

883
01:09:51,204 --> 01:09:53,403
In Al-Mughni(ألمغني) it states that Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) said:

884
01:09:53,950 --> 01:09:58,520
There is nothing comparable in rewards to meeting the enemy.

885
01:09:59,391 --> 01:10:04,086
And for one to involve in the actual fighting is the best of deeds.

886
01:10:04,878 --> 01:10:06,801
And this is compared to supportive roles.

887
01:10:07,451 --> 01:10:11,172
So again, there's nothing comparable in rewards to meeting the enemy.

888
01:10:11,511 --> 01:10:14,791
And for one to involve in the actual fighting is the best of deeds,

889
01:10:15,235 --> 01:10:18,957
the ones who are fighting the enemy, are the ones defending Islam.

890
01:10:19,257 --> 01:10:20,955
So what can be greater than that.

891
01:10:21,455 --> 01:10:27,769
People feel safe, while they feel fear, they have given up their souls for Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

892
01:10:28,269 --> 01:10:31,009
These are the words of Imam Ahmad رضي الله عنه.

893
01:10:31,377 --> 01:10:34,410
Jihad(جهاد) is the most beloved deed to Allah.

894
01:10:34,710 --> 01:10:40,532
Now when we were talking about the best deed, you find the some Ahadith(احاديث), It says Jihad(جهاد).

895
01:10:41,868 --> 01:10:46,241
In some Ahadith(احاديث), it says: Being dutiful towards your parents.

896
01:10:46,756 --> 01:10:49,658
There's some Ahadith(احاديث) it that says: Zikr(زكر) of Allah,

897
01:10:50,834 --> 01:10:53,310
another Hadith(حديث), it would says: Eeman(ايمان) in Allah.

898
01:10:53,762 --> 01:10:55,575
How do you reconcile between this?

899
01:10:56,708 --> 01:10:58,376
I mean, the best thing should be the best deed.

900
01:10:58,476 --> 01:11:03,273
Yani(يعني) you can't have more than one thing that all of them are the best.

901
01:11:04,082 --> 01:11:05,105
How do you reconcile.?

902
01:11:06,429 --> 01:11:09,023
Tayeb(طيِّب) that's one way to reconcile, for example,

903
01:11:09,523 --> 01:11:14,097
when one man came to Rasool Ullah, and this was a tough man married to nine women.

904
01:11:14,463 --> 01:11:17,126
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him first of all you have to divorce five,

905
01:11:17,426 --> 01:11:19,287
and then you got to Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

906
01:11:20,029 --> 01:11:22,621
Another man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, he was old in age,

907
01:11:23,021 --> 01:11:25,747
He told him: O Rasool Ullah tell me what to do? Rasool Ullah told him: Make zikr(زكر).

908
01:11:27,225 --> 01:11:34,818
So, the context of these two people, is clear that Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving them an answer according to their ability.

909
01:11:35,218 --> 01:11:36,790
Is there another way to reconcile.?

910
01:11:36,990 --> 01:11:38,871
What about it.?

911
01:11:40,002 --> 01:11:44,286
So the Ayah(آية) makes it clear that Jihad(جهاد) is the best.

912
01:11:45,514 --> 01:11:51,040
Tayeb(طيِّب) there is an argument placed by one of the scholars that because of this Ayah(آية),

913
01:11:51,510 --> 01:11:55,384
and also the first Ayah(آية) that we read that the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is better than the Qaid(قائد)

914
01:11:56,115 --> 01:12:00,245
that there is a deed, that is, that is the best in general.

915
01:12:01,196 --> 01:12:05,570
But then there are other deeds that are better in specific situations.

916
01:12:05,770 --> 01:12:08,834
So there's one deed, that is the best.

917
01:12:10,159 --> 01:12:14,326
And then there are other deeds that are in exceptional situations, the best.

918
01:12:15,126 --> 01:12:18,405
And the argument is based on the fact that the Ayah(آية), the Ayah(آية) of a As-Saff(ألصف),

919
01:12:18,505 --> 01:12:24,505
and the Ayah(آية) of An-Nisa(ألنساء) state that the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is better than the Qaaid(قائد).

920
01:12:24,605 --> 01:12:28,112
So, this gives a general rule, this establishes a general rule.

921
01:12:29,782 --> 01:12:33,915
The  exceptions to that rule are situations where a person is not able to do Jihad(جهاد).

922
01:12:33,978 --> 01:12:46,257
So, then, in other specific situations, so you'd have something like being dutiful towards the parents, or making a Zikr(زكر) or Hajj(حَجْ).

923
01:12:46,557 --> 01:12:47,723
Like for example with a women.

924
01:12:48,990 --> 01:12:55,858
And this opinion would make more sense because the Ayaat(آيات) of Quran do set the rule,

925
01:12:56,603 --> 01:13:03,438
and Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an make it clear that in general Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) is the best of all deeds.

926
01:13:04,438 --> 01:13:07,425
Abdullah Bin Salam(عبدالله بن سلام), said:

927
01:13:08,661 --> 01:13:14,630
We were a group of the companions and Abdullah Bin Salam(عبدالله بن سلام) is the Jewish Rabbi, who became Muslim,

928
01:13:15,678 --> 01:13:16,591
Abdullah Bin Salam(عبدالله بن سلام).

929
01:13:18,711 --> 01:13:23,322
And Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him Shahadah(شَهَادَة) of Jannah(جنة), he is in Jannah(جنة).

930
01:13:26,738 --> 01:13:31,332
He says we were a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, and we said:

931
01:13:31,481 --> 01:13:35,260
If we just knew what was the most beloved deed to Allah.

932
01:13:35,695 --> 01:13:36,833
Allah then revealed:

933
01:13:36,933 --> 01:13:44,209
سَبَّحَ لِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الأَرضِ ۖ وَهُوَ العَزيزُ الحَكيمُ ۞

934
01:13:44,709 --> 01:13:52,074
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا لِمَ تَقولونَ ما لا تَفعَلونَ ۞

935
01:13:52,574 --> 01:13:59,298
كَبُرَ مَقتًا عِندَ اللَّهِ أَن تَقولوا ما لا تَفعَلونَ ۞

936
01:13:59,798 --> 01:14:06,916
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِهِ صَفًّا

937
01:14:07,449 --> 01:14:13,552
صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُم بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ۞

938
01:14:13,901 --> 01:14:18,880
Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth exalts Allah

939
01:14:19,180 --> 01:14:21,601
and He is the Exalted in Might, and Wise.

940
01:14:21,701 --> 01:14:25,944
Oh you, who have believed: Why do you say, what you do not do.

941
01:14:26,344 --> 01:14:32,139
Great is hatred in the sight of Allah that you say, but you do not do.

942
01:14:32,288 --> 01:14:35,542
Indeed, Allah loves those, who fight in his cause in a row,

943
01:14:35,799 --> 01:14:39,505
as though they are a single structure joined firmly.

944
01:14:39,905 --> 01:14:47,591
So Allah is saying that the deed that He loves most is that you fight in rank joined firmly.

945
01:14:49,361 --> 01:14:55,480
And the Hadith(حديث) itself in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Bayhaqi(بيهقي), Al-Hakim(ألحاكم) and Ibn-e-Mubarak(إبن مبارك).

946
01:14:56,030 --> 01:15:00,373
The Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is the greatest of all people, Allah says:

947
01:15:00,873 --> 01:15:13,971
لا يَستَوِي القاعِدونَ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ غَيرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ وَالمُجاهِدونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم ۚ

948
01:15:14,734 --> 01:15:23,686
فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ المُجاهِدينَ بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم عَلَى القاعِدينَ دَرَجَةً ۚ

949
01:15:24,086 --> 01:15:28,399
وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الحُسنىٰ ۚ

950
01:15:28,699 --> 01:15:35,568
وَفَضَّلَ اللَّهُ المُجاهِدينَ عَلَى القاعِدينَ أَجرًا عَظيمًا۞

951
01:15:36,168 --> 01:15:41,693
دَرَجاتٍ مِنهُ وَمَغفِرَةً وَرَحمَةً ۚ

952
01:15:41,993 --> 01:15:45,937
وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفورًا رَحيمًا۞

953
01:15:46,337 --> 01:15:50,959
Allah has preferred the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) over those, who remain behind, with the great reward.

954
01:15:51,259 --> 01:15:54,014
Degrees from Him and forgiveness and mercy.

955
01:15:54,374 --> 01:15:56,585
And Allah is Ever forgiving and Merciful.

956
01:15:56,929 --> 01:15:59,356
An-Nisa(ألنِّساء) Verse 95 and 96.

957
01:16:00,170 --> 01:16:03,295
Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked in this Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم),

958
01:16:03,906 --> 01:16:05,214
who is the best of people?

959
01:16:05,274 --> 01:16:12,038
He said: A believer who is making Jihad(جهاد) with his life and his wealth, in the cause of Allah.

960
01:16:12,438 --> 01:16:13,378
The next heading:

961
01:16:14,158 --> 01:16:17,990
No one can practice any act of worship, equivalent to Jihad(جهاد).

962
01:16:19,392 --> 01:16:20,487
In Sahih Muslim(صحيح ألمسلم)

963
01:16:21,970 --> 01:16:26,665
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrates that the Messenger of Allah was asked about a deed equal in reward to Jihad(جهاد),

964
01:16:26,733 --> 01:16:28,679
he replied, You cannot do it.

965
01:16:29,628 --> 01:16:30,648
They asked again.

966
01:16:31,048 --> 01:16:35,273
And then a third time, and every time the Messenger of Allah would say you cannot do it.

967
01:16:36,775 --> 01:16:41,135
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: The equivalent of the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), is the one who fasts

968
01:16:41,461 --> 01:16:45,651
and prays continuously without resting until the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) comes back.

969
01:16:45,738 --> 01:16:47,519
And we did talk about this Hadith(حديث) yesterday,

970
01:16:48,183 --> 01:16:50,125
so I'll skip the others that are similar to it.

971
01:16:51,187 --> 01:16:54,845
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) says, this is a statement by Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره),

972
01:16:55,265 --> 01:17:00,820
he says: The horse of the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), would be running in a pasture land,

973
01:17:01,560 --> 01:17:04,257
and the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) would be given rewards for that.

974
01:17:05,171 --> 01:17:10,281
His horse is just roaming around, and the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) would be rewarded for that.

975
01:17:10,841 --> 01:17:16,101
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: If the ones, with high aspirations,

976
01:17:16,805 --> 01:17:22,126
those who had their rewards multiplied because of their companionship of the Messenger of Allah.

977
01:17:22,677 --> 01:17:28,988
If they cannot find anything equivalent to Jihad(جهاد), then how can we be at ease with lower deeds.?

978
01:17:29,588 --> 01:17:35,898
How can we settle for other deeds, when even then, we might have the mixed with insincerity and shortcomings.

979
01:17:36,336 --> 01:17:41,927
Oh Allah wake us up from this sleep and grant us Jihad(جهاد) in your cause before it's too late.

980
01:17:42,550 --> 01:17:47,152
You are our hope for any good, and there is no strength with anyone but You.

981
01:17:48,099 --> 01:17:54,088
He is saying that the Sahabah(صحابه), who are with Rasool Allah ﷺ, they never gave up Jihad(جهاد),

982
01:17:54,188 --> 01:17:58,583
even though they were the highest status of being companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ, living with him.

983
01:17:59,309 --> 01:18:00,570
So what are we to do.?

984
01:18:01,845 --> 01:18:02,742
The next heading:

985
01:18:03,350 --> 01:18:10,980
References that the sleep of the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is better than the praying of the night, and fasting of the day, for others.

986
01:18:11,682 --> 01:18:15,044
Safwan Bin Saleem(صفوان بن سليم) said: Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) asked:

987
01:18:15,730 --> 01:18:22,516
Can any one of you pray continuously without rest, and fast continuously without a break,

988
01:18:22,916 --> 01:18:25,858
they said: O Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره), who could do that.

989
01:18:26,158 --> 01:18:32,176
He said: I swear in the name of Allah, the sleep of the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is better than that.

990
01:18:33,303 --> 01:18:38,549
So other people would be praying the whole night fasting the day struggling in Ibadah(عبادة)

991
01:18:38,925 --> 01:18:41,655
and the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is asleep, and it's still making more Ajr(أجْر).

992
01:18:42,127 --> 01:18:46,737
What about if the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) would spend the night, in worshipping Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and fasting the day?

993
01:18:48,049 --> 01:18:51,135
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس), he actually says: If this is the status of their sleep.

994
01:18:51,279 --> 01:18:52,489
Then what about their prayers.

995
01:18:52,889 --> 01:18:58,139
This is what the competitors should compete for, and this is what others should cry for missing.

996
01:18:58,961 --> 01:18:59,885
The next heading:

997
01:19:00,085 --> 01:19:05,185
Allah reserved 100 levels in paradise for the Mujahideen(مجاهدين)

998
01:19:05,685 --> 01:19:09,774
between each level and the other is the distance between the heavens and earth.

999
01:19:11,886 --> 01:19:14,775
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) states that the Messenger of Allah said:

1000
01:19:15,550 --> 01:19:20,889
There are 100 levels in paradise, especially prepared by Allah for the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

1001
01:19:21,476 --> 01:19:27,199
In His cause between each level and the next is the difference between the heaven and earth.

1002
01:19:28,069 --> 01:19:32,217
So when you ask Allah asked him to grant you, Al-firdous(ألفردوس),

1003
01:19:32,517 --> 01:19:35,148
it is in the middle of Paradise and the highest part of it,

1004
01:19:35,848 --> 01:19:40,014
from it, the rivers of paradise spring and above it is the Throne of Allah.

1005
01:19:40,517 --> 01:19:41,759
This is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

1006
01:19:42,965 --> 01:19:45,281
Are you fine, we carry on, you're not getting tired.?

1007
01:19:46,846 --> 01:19:48,333
The next heading:

1008
01:19:48,433 --> 01:19:51,826
The Rahbania(رهبانية) and Siyaha(سياحة) of this Ummah(امة) is Jihad(جهاد).

1009
01:19:52,126 --> 01:19:53,784
What is the Rahbania(رهبانية)? And what is Siyaha(سياحة)?

1010
01:19:54,581 --> 01:19:58,390
Rahbania(رهبانية) is monetarism,

1011
01:19:59,531 --> 01:20:05,772
some Christian Orders, used to practice Rahbania(رهبانية).

1012
01:20:06,139 --> 01:20:13,211
Rahbania(رهبانية) is when they, we would say, Divorce this world, so they will not get married.

1013
01:20:14,839 --> 01:20:21,147
And they would not enjoy food and drink, and they will stay away from all of the fittan(فتن) of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

1014
01:20:22,479 --> 01:20:26,287
And they would lock themselves up in monasteries,

1015
01:20:26,848 --> 01:20:32,837
in caves, in mountain peaks, devoting their time to worshiping Allah.

1016
01:20:34,569 --> 01:20:39,666
So it's a very tough lifestyle and they're doing it for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1017
01:20:40,234 --> 01:20:45,684
Now Allah says in Qur'an that this was something that wasn't prescribed on them.

1018
01:20:46,627 --> 01:20:50,318
They did it, but Allah did not ordered them to do it.

1019
01:20:51,131 --> 01:20:56,942
But it was very prevalent among specially Eastern Christians,

1020
01:20:57,581 --> 01:20:59,774
you know among Western Christians, they are not into this.

1021
01:21:01,310 --> 01:21:08,561
There is more materialism, in the West, for them to follow that truth and that's why you would find in the Hadith(حديث).

1022
01:21:10,232 --> 01:21:13,449
It says the Romans, it doesn't say the Christians, even though they are Christian,

1023
01:21:14,149 --> 01:21:18,854
because Christianity for the West is more of an identity and association,

1024
01:21:19,731 --> 01:21:21,616
than it is something that is practiced,

1025
01:21:21,816 --> 01:21:27,953
Just like when Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was told about this Christian Arab tribe of Tae(طئ),

1026
01:21:28,653 --> 01:21:32,424
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: They know nothing about Christianity except drinking wine.

1027
01:21:32,924 --> 01:21:35,979
They're not religious people, that's all they know about Christianity.

1028
01:21:36,786 --> 01:21:46,422
So, this Ta'abud(تعبد), monotheism existed among the Eastern Christians like for example in Abyssinia,

1029
01:21:46,705 --> 01:21:48,978
Egypt, Syria, Turkey.

1030
01:21:51,136 --> 01:21:55,607
There were many of these Rahban(رهبان), who devoted themselves to worshiping, and Ibadah(عبادة).

1031
01:21:57,403 --> 01:22:03,903
And it is something that some of Sahabah(صحابه) looked up to in the beginning of the Da'wah(دعوة),

1032
01:22:03,948 --> 01:22:10,829
it is said that some of the Sahabah(صحابه), were thinking about leading a life of Rahbania(رهبانية),

1033
01:22:11,229 --> 01:22:15,258
but then Rasool Allah ﷺ, prohibited them from doing that.

1034
01:22:16,013 --> 01:22:22,854
And then we also have the Hadith(حديث) of the three men who came to ask the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ about his life at home.

1035
01:22:23,861 --> 01:22:30,120
So, one of them said: I don't marry woman, the other one said: I don't sleep and the other one said: I never break my fast.

1036
01:22:30,710 --> 01:22:36,724
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: But I fast, some days and don't fast others.

1037
01:22:37,171 --> 01:22:39,666
And I pray part of the night and I sleep.

1038
01:22:40,182 --> 01:22:42,319
And I marry women, and that is my Sunnah(سنة).

1039
01:22:42,802 --> 01:22:45,637
And whoever is different than my Sunnah(سنة), doesn't belong to me.

1040
01:22:47,094 --> 01:22:48,268
Then there is Siyaha(سياحة),

1041
01:22:49,234 --> 01:22:51,920
Siyaha(سياحة) is similar to Rahbania(رهبانية), but they would travel.

1042
01:22:53,362 --> 01:22:55,737
So these were people who didn't have a fixed base,

1043
01:22:55,985 --> 01:22:58,445
they didn't have a home, they don't have families,

1044
01:22:59,251 --> 01:23:02,624
they just traveled in the earth contemplating the creation of Allah.

1045
01:23:04,342 --> 01:23:06,642
Now the word Siyaha(سياحة) in Arabic mean travelling.

1046
01:23:08,417 --> 01:23:10,621
And now, tourism is called Siyaha(سياحة).

1047
01:23:12,170 --> 01:23:17,138
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: That the Rahbania(رهبانية) and Siyaha(سياحة) of this Ummah(امة) is Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1048
01:23:18,200 --> 01:23:20,379
In other words Rahbania(رهبانية) is replaced

1049
01:23:20,759 --> 01:23:23,712
and Siyaha(سياحة) is replaced with Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1050
01:23:24,436 --> 01:23:29,700
So we're not allowed to do Rahbania(رهبانية) and Siyaha(سياحة) anymore but we should do Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1051
01:23:31,654 --> 01:23:34,816
A man came to the Messenger of Allah and said: Advise me!

1052
01:23:35,425 --> 01:23:39,903
He said: Have Taqwa(تقوى) of Allah, since it is the essence of our good

1053
01:23:40,667 --> 01:23:44,423
and make Jihad(جهاد), since it is the monotheism of this nation.

1054
01:23:45,039 --> 01:23:50,040
And remember Allah and recite Qur'an since it is light for you in this world,

1055
01:23:50,340 --> 01:23:56,000
and remembrance for you in the heavens and preserve your tongue except from Good.

1056
01:23:56,300 --> 01:23:58,543
For you would then defeat Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

1057
01:23:59,032 --> 01:24:01,814
Abu Abdullah Al-Halimi(ابوعبدالله ألحليمي), he says:

1058
01:24:02,555 --> 01:24:06,210
The meaning of the monotheism of this nation is Jihad(جهاد).

1059
01:24:06,381 --> 01:24:12,195
Is that the Christians used to practice monotheism by leading a secluded life in a monastery,

1060
01:24:12,592 --> 01:24:18,557
the maximum sacrifice they would give to Allah, is to stay away from the allurements of this world,

1061
01:24:18,857 --> 01:24:21,888
they would claim that they are staying away from everyone,

1062
01:24:22,188 --> 01:24:24,568
in order not to harm anyone,

1063
01:24:25,529 --> 01:24:30,290
but there is no harm, greater than leaving the evildoers practice their evil.

1064
01:24:30,725 --> 01:24:37,208
Therefore, the real ones, who are avoiding evil and harm, are the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) who are stamping evil out.

1065
01:24:39,187 --> 01:24:43,741
So, Rahban(رهبان), they stayed in the monastery so that they can stay away from evil.

1066
01:24:44,404 --> 01:24:48,250
But with this Ummah(امة), you stay away from evil by destroying it.

1067
01:24:49,206 --> 01:24:52,615
So that's the difference between this Ummah(امة) and the Ummam(امم) before.

1068
01:24:54,088 --> 01:24:56,351
Because see evil will never leave you alone.

1069
01:24:57,009 --> 01:25:02,668
It will keep on encroaching on your territory, until it eliminates you.

