 that come out in the west, every now and then once they tell you that vegetables are good for you,

1249
01:39:04,765 --> 01:39:06,548
sometimes they tell wine is good for you.

1250
01:39:06,963 --> 01:39:12,342
Just like for example when it comes to infants in America,

1251
01:39:13,497 --> 01:39:18,141
a while ago, they used to tell mothers.

1252
01:39:18,914 --> 01:39:27,053
You should have your newborn child sleep on their stomach, on the stomach, that's the most healthy way of sleeping,

1253
01:39:28,910 --> 01:39:36,276
 but Rasool Allah ﷺ says that, that is the posture of the people of hellfire, the sleeping on the stomach.

1254
01:39:37,825 --> 01:39:41,555
Now, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) in America, they're telling women,

1255
01:39:42,483 --> 01:39:47,620
Don't have your child sleep on your stomach because that's a reason for sudden infant death. S.I.D.

1256
01:39:48,020 --> 01:39:50,249
You should have them either sleep on the side or the back.

1257
01:39:52,408 --> 01:39:55,266
So the thing is here. Do you follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

1258
01:39:55,343 --> 01:40:00,779
or do you follow what the every theory that comes up now and then.

1259
01:40:01,994 --> 01:40:06,848
One should trust in, what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says and the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

1260
01:40:07,162 --> 01:40:09,053
and you can never go wrong with that.

1261
01:40:09,653 --> 01:40:15,715
And I've noticed this as among some brothers, they're making meat Haram(حرام) on themselves.

1262
01:40:17,010 --> 01:40:22,389
Actually one brother said that I have refrained completely from meat, I don't eat meat anymore.

1263
01:40:22,428 --> 01:40:23,018
I told him, why?

1264
01:40:23,376 --> 01:40:24,555
He said: Because it's not healthy.

1265
01:40:24,855 --> 01:40:26,859
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not eat meat and all that stuff.

1266
01:40:26,915 --> 01:40:29,196
Where did you get that from that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not eat meat.?

1267
01:40:29,928 --> 01:40:35,191
In fact the staple of the people in Arabia was meat and bread, barley bread that was their food.

1268
01:40:36,720 --> 01:40:38,748
So don't make anything Haram(حرام) on yourself.

1269
01:40:38,804 --> 01:40:44,404
When Rasool Allah ﷺ make Asal(عسل), Honey Haram(حرام) on himself, the Ayaat(آيات) of Tahrim(تحريم) were revealed,

1270
01:40:44,804 --> 01:40:48,721
يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ لِمَ تُحَرِّمُ مَا أَحَلَّ اللَّهُ لَكَ تَبْتَغِي مَرْضَاتَ أَزْوَاجِكَ

1271
01:40:49,321 --> 01:40:52,739
O Messenger of Allah, Why are you making what is Halal(حلال), Haram(حرام) on yourself.

1272
01:40:53,298 --> 01:40:57,943
These are Tayibaat(طيبات), all are Tayibaat(طيبات). One should just eat in moderation.

1273
01:40:58,582 --> 01:41:01,266
I'll read the exact wording of the Hadith(حديث).

1274
01:41:02,166 --> 01:41:06,952
Jabir Ibn Abdullah(جابربن عبدالله) narrates: We were sent on an expedition by the Messenger of Allah,

1275
01:41:07,352 --> 01:41:09,486
to raid the caravan owned by Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

1276
01:41:10,333 --> 01:41:12,560
and he appointed Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) as our leader,

1277
01:41:13,042 --> 01:41:18,758
the Messenger of Allah found nothing to provide us with except leather bags filled with dates and nothing else.

1278
01:41:19,358 --> 01:41:21,883
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) would then hand us one date each.

1279
01:41:22,183 --> 01:41:24,747
The narrator was asked what good would that be.

1280
01:41:25,394 --> 01:41:27,787
He said: We would eat it and then suck on the date seed.

1281
01:41:28,187 --> 01:41:32,245
In addition to drinking water that was the only food we would have for the whole day.

1282
01:41:33,045 --> 01:41:36,542
Then we would gather leaves of trees and soak them in water and eat them.

1283
01:41:37,086 --> 01:41:39,108
Then we headed for the direction of the coast.

1284
01:41:39,508 --> 01:41:43,343
We saw what appeared like a sand dune and to our surprise it was a whale.

1285
01:41:43,943 --> 01:41:47,360
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) at first said: It is dead, therefore it cannot be consumed.

1286
01:41:47,760 --> 01:41:51,954
He then said: But we are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah, and we are in the Cause of Allah,

1287
01:41:52,230 --> 01:41:54,059
and this is a necessity, so eat from it.

1288
01:41:54,520 --> 01:41:58,324
We stayed there for a whole month eating from it, until we grew fat,

1289
01:41:58,792 --> 01:42:00,473
and we were 300 in number,

1290
01:42:01,073 --> 01:42:08,158
we would collect oil from its eyes with buckets and cut from its flesh pieces as large as a bull.

1291
01:42:08,758 --> 01:42:12,068
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) had us fit 13 men in its eye socket.

1292
01:42:12,568 --> 01:42:17,098
He then had one of its rib bones fixed to the ground, like an arc.

1293
01:42:17,931 --> 01:42:26,143
Then he had the tallest camel with us, pass from under it, without the camel touching the bone.

1294
01:42:26,743 --> 01:42:32,971
We then picked up, dried meat, to carry with us to Madina.

1295
01:42:33,426 --> 01:42:35,509
When we told the Messenger of Allah, our story.

1296
01:42:35,609 --> 01:42:37,649
He said: That was sustenance, Allah sent for you.

1297
01:42:38,049 --> 01:42:41,425
Do you have any of that meat left with you to give me some.

1298
01:42:41,685 --> 01:42:43,861
We sent some to him and he ate from it.

1299
01:42:44,561 --> 01:42:45,801
This is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح ألمسلم).

1300
01:42:46,401 --> 01:42:52,722
Miscellaneous rewards for the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), Allah says:

1301
01:42:53,022 --> 01:42:59,793
ما كانَ لِأَهلِ المَدينَةِ وَمَن حَولَهُم مِنَ الأَعرابِ أَن

1302
01:43:00,011 --> 01:43:08,400
أَن يَتَخَلَّفوا عَن رَسولِ اللَّهِ وَلا يَرغَبوا بِأَنفُسِهِم عَن نَفسِهِ ۚ

1303
01:43:08,800 --> 01:43:16,059
ذٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُم لا يُصيبُهُم ظَمَأٌ وَلا نَصَبٌ وَلا

1304
01:43:16,390 --> 01:43:25,274
وَلا مَخمَصَةٌ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَلا يَطَئونَ مَوطِئًا يَغيظُ الكُفّارَ

1305
01:43:25,666 --> 01:43:33,968
وَلا يَنالونَ مِن عَدُوٍّ نَيلًا إِلّا كُتِبَ لَهُم بِهِ عَمَلٌ صالِحٌ ۚ

1306
01:43:34,268 --> 01:43:38,982
إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُضيعُ أَجرَ المُحسِنينَ ۞

1307
01:43:39,282 --> 01:43:47,282
وَلا يُنفِقونَ نَفَقَةً صَغيرَةً وَلا كَبيرَةً وَلا

1308
01:43:47,495 --> 01:43:57,157
وَلا يَقطَعونَ وادِيًا إِلّا كُتِبَ لَهُم لِيَجزِيَهُمُ اللَّهُ أَحسَنَ ما كانوا يَعمَلونَ۞

1309
01:43:57,617 --> 01:44:04,155
That is because they are not afflicted by thirst or fatigue or hunger in the cause of Allah,

1310
01:44:04,855 --> 01:44:09,129
nor do they tread on any ground that enrages the disbelievers,

1311
01:44:09,449 --> 01:44:16,704
nor do they inflict upon an enemy any infliction, but that it is registered for them as righteous deed.

1312
01:44:17,304 --> 01:44:22,053
Indeed, Allah does not allow to be lost the reward of the doers of good.

1313
01:44:23,153 --> 01:44:28,578
Nor do they spend an expenditure, small or large, or cross a valley,

1314
01:44:28,861 --> 01:44:34,755
but that it is registered for them, that Allah may reward them for the best of what they were doing.

1315
01:44:35,406 --> 01:44:40,614
At-Toba(التوبة) Verse 120 and 121.

1316
01:44:44,487 --> 01:44:46,825
Abu Bakr Bin Abu Musa(أبوبكر بن أبوموسى) narrates:

1317
01:44:47,395 --> 01:44:50,970
I heard my father say that the Messenger of Allah said:

1318
01:44:51,522 --> 01:44:55,014
The gates of paradise are lying under the swords.

1319
01:44:56,022 --> 01:44:58,660
A poor man with rags stood up and said:

1320
01:44:59,260 --> 01:45:02,817
O, Abu Musa(أبوموسى), Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah.?

1321
01:45:03,725 --> 01:45:04,990
My father said: Yes!

1322
01:45:05,201 --> 01:45:08,782
The man went back to his company and told them, I give you my Salam(سلام).

1323
01:45:09,228 --> 01:45:15,531
He then broke his sword, sheath and marched towards the enemy striking them with a sword until he was killed.

1324
01:45:16,171 --> 01:45:18,650
So this is Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) speaking in a mosque,

1325
01:45:19,097 --> 01:45:21,748
he said: That Jannah(جنة) is under the shade of swords.

1326
01:45:22,192 --> 01:45:25,772
So this man heard that and he said: Did you hear this from Rasool Ullah.?

1327
01:45:26,072 --> 01:45:27,313
Abu Musa(أبوموسى) said: Yes!

1328
01:45:27,613 --> 01:45:29,195
He went and fought, until he was killed.

1329
01:45:30,437 --> 01:45:33,157
What does Ibn Daqeeq Al-Eid(إبن دقيق ألعيد) say about this Hadith(حديث)?

1330
01:45:33,388 --> 01:45:33,904
He said:

1331
01:45:34,926 --> 01:45:39,264
The statement that the gates of paradise are lying under the swords,

1332
01:45:39,703 --> 01:45:44,333
would mean that paradise is attained through the swords of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين),

1333
01:45:45,062 --> 01:45:49,268
and using the sword is necessary to get paradise and to open its gates,

1334
01:45:50,378 --> 01:45:52,995
as if the sword is the key to Jannah(جنة).

1335
01:45:53,786 --> 01:46:00,192
The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever fights in the cause of Allah, the time it takes to milk a camel is granted paradise.

1336
01:46:01,095 --> 01:46:06,136
And this is in Ahmed(أحمد), Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Ibn Majah(إبن ماجه) and Ibn Habban(إبن حَبَّان).

1337
01:46:07,384 --> 01:46:10,743
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

1338
01:46:11,518 --> 01:46:17,107
The trials and tribulations are on their way, trials like pieces of a dark night,

1339
01:46:17,740 --> 01:46:23,561
the safest from them would be a man living on the peaks of mountains, living off his flock of sheep

1340
01:46:24,061 --> 01:46:27,987
or a man mounting his horse, living off his sword.

1341
01:46:29,281 --> 01:46:29,925
 Al-Hakim(ألحاكم).

1342
01:46:31,820 --> 01:46:35,586
So in the times of Fitan(فتن), only two people will be safe.

1343
01:46:37,187 --> 01:46:40,433
The Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), who is riding hs horse fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

1344
01:46:41,040 --> 01:46:47,932
and the one who avoids all of the Fitan(فتن) and goes and lives off his sheep, the peaks of mountains.

1345
01:46:48,468 --> 01:46:52,583
Everyone else will be consumed by the Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

1346
01:46:54,624 --> 01:47:00,029
Subura(صَبُورا) narrated, I heard the Messenger of Allah say:

1347
01:47:00,329 --> 01:47:05,725
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) has intercepted the son of Adam(آدم) on his path towards Islam and told him.

1348
01:47:06,516 --> 01:47:12,265
Are you going to become Muslim, and leave your heritage and the religion of your forefathers.

1349
01:47:12,919 --> 01:47:16,567
But the son of Adam(آدم) disobeyed him and became a Muslim and was forgiven.

1350
01:47:17,067 --> 01:47:20,168
Then Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) sat for him, on his path to Hijrah(هجرة) and told him:

1351
01:47:20,715 --> 01:47:23,937
Will you make Hijrah(هجرة) and leave behind your home and land.?

1352
01:47:24,948 --> 01:47:27,373
He disobeyed him and made Hijrah(هجرة).

1353
01:47:28,848 --> 01:47:32,088
He then sat for him on his path towards Jihad(جهاد) and told him:

1354
01:47:32,588 --> 01:47:36,519
Are you going to fight when it's an exhaustion of yourself, and your wealth,

1355
01:47:37,055 --> 01:47:42,325
you would go to kill, and you would be killed, and then your wife would be taken and the wealth divided,

1356
01:47:42,925 --> 01:47:45,383
the son of Adam(آدم) disobeyed him and went on Jihad(جهاد),

1357
01:47:46,081 --> 01:47:47,820
the Messenger of Allah, then said:

1358
01:47:48,162 --> 01:47:53,076
Whoever does that, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to paradise.

1359
01:47:53,631 --> 01:47:57,648
Or if he dies by his animals striking him, he would go to paradise.

1360
01:47:59,791 --> 01:48:03,113
So Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) keeps on interrupting you.

1361
01:48:04,934 --> 01:48:09,480
When you become Muslim, when you make Hijrah(هجرة), and anyone you make Jihad(جهاد).

1362
01:48:10,891 --> 01:48:14,582
Now brothers: Pay close attention to this statement.

1363
01:48:15,859 --> 01:48:22,377
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: If I were to marry a beautiful woman, whom I love,

1364
01:48:23,583 --> 01:48:30,429
or if I were given the good news of having a newborn son.

1365
01:48:31,584 --> 01:48:39,558
It is less beloved and dear to my heart, than to be in a cold icy night in an army,

1366
01:48:39,958 --> 01:48:42,643
waiting to meet the enemy, the next morning.

1367
01:48:43,325 --> 01:48:45,449
I advise you to go on Jihad(جهاد).

1368
01:48:46,513 --> 01:48:49,151
These were the words of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) before he died.

1369
01:48:51,641 --> 01:48:58,588
Now, brother, if I were to marry a beautiful woman whom I love,

1370
01:49:00,928 --> 01:49:06,426
or if I were given the good news of having a newborn son.

1371
01:49:08,687 --> 01:49:21,948
It is less beloved and dear to my heart, than to be in a cold icy night, in an army waiting to meet the enemy, the next morning,

1372
01:49:24,421 --> 01:49:27,367
I advise you to go on Jihad(جهاد).

1373
01:49:28,862 --> 01:49:41,023
The brothers who are married, if you can go back to the memory of the day you got married.

1374
01:49:43,582 --> 01:49:49,742
If you love your wife and you got married.

1375
01:49:51,016 --> 01:49:51,959
Think about that.

1376
01:49:53,581 --> 01:49:58,867
The brothers who have children. Think about the day when you had your new firstborn.

1377
01:49:59,649 --> 01:50:03,324
Think about the day you're given the news of having a newborn child.

1378
01:50:04,804 --> 01:50:06,275
These are days that you cannot forget.

1379
01:50:07,614 --> 01:50:14,849
These are events that make you the happiest on that day, you feel the top of the world.

1380
01:50:19,222 --> 01:50:21,390
These are natural human feelings.

1381
01:50:23,995 --> 01:50:28,694
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is saying: If I'm to marry a woman whom I love, and she's beautiful.

1382
01:50:29,735 --> 01:50:33,420
Or if I'm given the news of having a newborn son.

1383
01:50:34,911 --> 01:50:42,938
That is less dear to my heart, then spending a night in a tent and it's a very cold icy, windy night

1384
01:50:44,129 --> 01:50:46,151
and the next day in the morning I'm going to meet my enemy.

1385
01:50:49,431 --> 01:50:54,379
Do you see how much love that Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه had for Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

1386
01:50:55,543 --> 01:51:03,517
for you to love, Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), and not just Jihad(جهاد), you're in the middle of it.

1387
01:51:04,173 --> 01:51:07,541
And it's a cold, icy windy night.

1388
01:51:08,666 --> 01:51:12,369
Now, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is not a soldier in the army.

1389
01:51:13,343 --> 01:51:16,471
And by just being a soldier in the moment is tantalizing itself,

1390
01:51:16,946 --> 01:51:19,597
because you know that the next day you might not be living anymore.

1391
01:51:20,097 --> 01:51:24,702
You know that the next day you might be injured and in those days injuries, you know there's no anesthesia.

1392
01:51:25,202 --> 01:51:29,923
Nusayba Bint  Ka'ab(نُصيبة بنت كعب), who fought on Al-Yamamah(أليمامة), she said:

1393
01:51:30,375 --> 01:51:37,680
I left with 12 injuries in my body, and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was so kind and nice with us, Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

1394
01:51:38,380 --> 01:51:48,987
He appointed a physician to me, to come and take care of my wounds, and he would pour on my wounds boiling oil.

1395
01:51:50,299 --> 01:51:54,792
And the pain and suffering of the healing process was even worse than the injury itself.

1396
01:51:57,282 --> 01:52:02,844
Because in those days, there's no anesthesia, there's no anti bacteria so what they would use is boiling oil.

1397
01:52:03,791 --> 01:52:07,218
What it does is? Its seals the injury, and it kills the infection.

1398
01:52:11,142 --> 01:52:16,936
Now, some people before they go to the dentist for days they're thinking about that poking of the needle.

1399
01:52:17,285 --> 01:52:18,455
Just poking of needle.

1400
01:52:19,015 --> 01:52:23,471
And it's an anesthesia needle, it is to take away the pain that will come after it,

1401
01:52:23,847 --> 01:52:25,580
and they would think about it for days.

1402
01:52:27,335 --> 01:52:30,547
The Sahabah(صحابه) knew very well where they're getting themselves into,

1403
01:52:30,647 --> 01:52:36,335
Nusayba Bint  Ka'ab(نُصيبة بنت كعب), she knew very well, the suffering and pain that she could get,

1404
01:52:36,435 --> 01:52:42,481
when she goes on fight, I mean in those days, I mean, swords and arrows and spears are piercing your body.

1405
01:52:43,975 --> 01:52:48,828
So the soldier, not Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) the leader, the soldier by just thinking,

1406
01:52:48,928 --> 01:52:54,694
imagine the pressure they're under you know tomorrow I might be killed, tomorrow I might be injured,

1407
01:52:55,650 --> 01:52:57,453
tomorrow I might be handicapped.

1408
01:52:59,804 --> 01:53:03,178
So they're under so much tension.

1409
01:53:04,288 --> 01:53:07,351
Now Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is not soldier, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), is leader of the army.

1410
01:53:08,465 --> 01:53:13,006
And as the leader of the Army, you are responsible for whatever happens the next day.

1411
01:53:14,709 --> 01:53:17,851
And the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) they love each other and the leader if he makes a mistake

1412
01:53:17,893 --> 01:53:20,911
and some of his brothers died because of that will feel a lot of pain.

1413
01:53:21,991 --> 01:53:25,838
And he is responsible for the victory or loss that would happen the next day.

1414
01:53:25,938 --> 01:53:28,074
It's Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was held responsible for that.

1415
01:53:28,174 --> 01:53:31,718
So think about the mental pressure, the psychological pressure he is going through.

1416
01:53:33,569 --> 01:53:40,658
And in those days, I mean the Muslims, they would take defeat very seriously, I mean they wouldn't accept it.

1417
01:53:40,715 --> 01:53:45,657
Now Muslims are desensitized, it doesn't make a difference anymore but in those days, it was a serious thing.

1418
01:53:46,777 --> 01:53:49,992
I mean when Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was appointed leader in Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) and he retreated,

1419
01:53:50,313 --> 01:53:52,092
and he went into Madina what happened.?

1420
01:53:53,111 --> 01:53:55,398
I mean, look at the spirit that the kids had in Madina,

1421
01:53:55,847 --> 01:53:59,749
those kids would go and throw rocks at the army, and they say,

1422
01:53:59,792 --> 01:54:00,692
أنتم الفراغون

1423
01:54:00,771 --> 01:54:01,976
You are the ones, who ran away.

1424
01:54:02,246 --> 01:54:07,049
Kids of today who are playing Playstation have no idea what's going around in the world

1425
01:54:07,149 --> 01:54:10,467
but in those days, even the children knew what was happening.

1426
01:54:11,296 --> 01:54:16,828
And imagine how painful it is for an army to come in and the kids are pelting you with rocks.

1427
01:54:17,879 --> 01:54:19,948
The kids of Madina are saying,

1428
01:54:19,998 --> 01:54:20,929
أنتم الفراغون

1429
01:54:21,000 --> 01:54:22,776
You are the ones who ran away from battle.

1430
01:54:23,308 --> 01:54:26,342
It wasn't remain until Rasool Allah ﷺ came for their defense and said,

1431
01:54:26,384 --> 01:54:27,317
بل هم القراهون

1432
01:54:27,816 --> 01:54:31,268
But they are the ones, who are retreating to attack again.

1433
01:54:33,179 --> 01:54:35,723
Otherwise those kids would have given them a very hard time.

1434
01:54:37,589 --> 01:54:40,827
This also shows you Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), that the Spirit that existed in Madina,

1435
01:54:41,467 --> 01:54:44,486
spirit of Jihad(جهاد), even the kids were involved in it.

1436
01:54:47,698 --> 01:54:52,850
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), is going through all of that pressure, he can't sleep the night, he has to plan.

1437
01:54:53,870 --> 01:54:57,801
He loves that more than marrying a beautiful woman that he loves,

1438
01:54:58,212 --> 01:54:59,697
or having a newborn child.

1439
01:55:00,392 --> 01:55:02,578
That is the love of Jihad(جهاد) that's on a different level.

1440
01:55:04,971 --> 01:55:08,751
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he said, and this is narrated by Ibn-e-Asakir(إبن عساكر).

1441
01:55:09,333 --> 01:55:15,471
I was prevented a lot of recitation of Qur'an because of my preoccupation, in Jihad(جهاد).

1442
01:55:18,532 --> 01:55:23,136
حرمنن جهاد من تلاوت كثير من القرآن

1443
01:55:25,531 --> 01:55:30,755
In fact, it is said that, when he would lead the Salah(صلاة), because the Ameer(أمير) of the army would lead the Salah(صلاة),

1444
01:55:31,430 --> 01:55:36,249
he will start in one Surah(سورة) and finish in another. He would confuse the Ayaat(آيات).

1445
01:55:38,040 --> 01:55:43,360
But then he said: The reason is because I'm preoccupied with Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1446
01:55:45,494 --> 01:55:49,459
References to the preference of Jihad(جهاد) over Hajj(حَجْ).

1447
01:55:52,708 --> 01:55:56,141
Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر), listen to what Ibn Umar(إبن عُمَر) says and this narrated by Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن المبارك),

1448
01:55:56,857 --> 01:55:59,869
and Ibn Abi Shaibah(إبن أبي شعيبة), and the narration is authentic.

1449
01:56:01,705 --> 01:56:03,145
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said:

1450
01:56:04,201 --> 01:56:07,850
One trip on Jihad(جهاد) is better than 50 Hajj(حَجْ).

1451
01:56:09,646 --> 01:56:14,394
This is Sahih(صحيح) narration, one trip on Jihad(جهاد) is better than 50 Hajj(حَجْ).

1452
01:56:16,017 --> 01:56:17,306
Dhirar Ibn Amr(ضرارإبن عمرو) said:

1453
01:56:17,848 --> 01:56:23,711
I have spent a very long time in Jihad(جهاد) and my heart was longing to Hajj(حَجْ).

1454
01:56:25,779 --> 01:56:30,604
I made my preparations to go, and then went to greet my brothers.

1455
01:56:30,804 --> 01:56:35,869
I visited Is'haq Ibn Abi Farwah(إسحاق إبن أبي فروة), one of the scholars, to give him farewell.

1456
01:56:37,195 --> 01:56:39,149
He asked me: Where are you going?

1457
01:56:40,037 --> 01:56:42,971
I said: I'm going to Hajj(حَجْ).

1458
01:56:44,162 --> 01:56:47,678
He said: Has your opinion on Jihad(جهاد) changed or what?

1459
01:56:48,805 --> 01:56:50,569
Did your opinion on Jihad(جهاد) changed?

1460
01:56:51,537 --> 01:56:56,722
He said: No! It's just that I have been here on Jihad(جهاد) for a long time.

1461
01:56:57,254 --> 01:57:00,211
Now I was longing for Hajj(حَجْ) and visiting the house of Allah,

1462
01:57:00,621 --> 01:57:07,077
you know, if you visited the house of Allah once you become addicted to it, you become hooked for life.

1463
01:57:08,360 --> 01:57:12,028
There's something about the house of Allah that attracts the hearts of the believer.

1464
01:57:13,657 --> 01:57:16,013
And that is because of the Dua(دُعَا) of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

1465
01:57:16,113 --> 01:57:18,094
فَاجْعَلْ أَفْئِدَةً مِنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِي إِلَيْهِمْ

1466
01:57:18,523 --> 01:57:22,612
Make the hearts of people rush towards the house of Allah.

1467
01:57:23,901 --> 01:57:26,124
Ibrahim عليه السّلام was told by Allah

1468
01:57:26,224 --> 01:57:27,458
أذن في الناس بالحج

1469
01:57:27,943 --> 01:57:30,973
Call the people to Hajj(حَجْ), make Adhan(آذَان), called the people to Hajj(حَجْ).

1470
01:57:31,294 --> 01:57:34,777
When he finished building the house of Allah, there was nobody living there.

1471
01:57:35,112 --> 01:57:35,953
It was empty.

1472
01:57:36,683 --> 01:57:39,701
And Allah is telling him to invite the people to Hajj(حَجْ), Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said:

1473
01:57:40,141 --> 01:57:46,129
Oh Allah, my voice is weak, and it cannot reach the people, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told him,

1474
01:57:46,185 --> 01:57:48,345
عليك ندا وعلينا عجابة

1475
01:57:49,027 --> 01:57:51,650
You will make the invitation, and we will convey it.

1476
01:57:52,915 --> 01:58:00,217
So now that call of Ibrahim عليه السّلام is being conveyed in every year by millions of Muslims, coming from every corner of the globe.

1477
01:58:03,303 --> 01:58:09,426
And as soon as you see the house of Allah once when you leave, you become homesick.

1478
01:58:10,064 --> 01:58:14,946
When you go back home, you become homesick because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

1479
01:58:15,046 --> 01:58:17,083
وَإِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ مَثَابَةً لِّلنَّاسِ

1480
01:58:17,755 --> 01:58:20,793
Masaba(مَثَابَةً) means something that you want to go back to frequently.

1481
01:58:21,653 --> 01:58:26,628
The house is Masaba(مَثَابَةً), you want to visit it again and again and again.

1482
01:58:27,274 --> 01:58:29,765
You leave you go back home, you feel homesick to the house of Allah.

1483
01:58:32,366 --> 01:58:39,230
It was said that Christian missionaries were working in Indonesia very hard to convert the people to Christianity.

1484
01:58:40,117 --> 01:58:42,124
So after some very hard work,

1485
01:58:43,864 --> 01:58:49,166
they were able to convince this man, this old man to become Christian, and they only did so

1486
01:58:49,596 --> 01:58:54,954
after they promised him that we will fulfill your wish, you make a wish. We will do it for you.

1487
01:58:56,000 --> 01:58:59,022
So when he became Christian they said: What's your wish. He said: To make Hajj(حَجْ).

1488
01:59:03,020 --> 01:59:09,284
This is an Indonesian see the connection that the people have to the house of Allah, even though they're miles and miles away.

1489
01:59:13,840 --> 01:59:19,612
You know, for the Indonesian Hajji(حجَّي) before it used to be an entire year to make Hajj(حَجْ),

1490
01:59:21,924 --> 01:59:23,893
six months going and six months coming back.

1491
01:59:25,167 --> 01:59:28,498
It wasn't an easy thing. Nevertheless, they would go to Hajj(حَجْ).

1492
01:59:29,834 --> 01:59:32,646
So this man is in Jihad(جهاد) and now he wants to go to the house of Allah, He said:

1493
01:59:32,688 --> 01:59:36,263
It's been a long time, I haven't seen the house of Allah I want to go.

1494
01:59:37,654 --> 01:59:43,801
He said: No, it's just that I have been here on Jihad(جهاد) for a long time,

1495
01:59:44,001 --> 01:59:46,477
and I was longing for Hajj(حَجْ) visiting the house of Allah.

1496
01:59:47,792 --> 01:59:55,377
He told me: O Dharar(ضرار), you should not do what you love, but you should do what Allah loves

1497
01:59:56,046 --> 01:59:57,784
and see Brothers its a very important thing.

1498
01:59:59,626 --> 02:00:03,168
You don't do what you want to do but you do what Allah wants you to do.

1499
02:00:04,848 --> 02:00:10,480
We always go with what our whims tell us, tell us, and I'm talking about Ibadaat(عبادات).

1500
02:00:11,806 --> 02:00:15,709
What if Allah has puts you in a Saghra(ثغرة), Allah has put you in a certain position.

1501
02:00:16,478 --> 02:00:19,185
Don't allow Islam to be attacked from that position.

1502
02:00:19,643 --> 02:00:22,246
It is your responsibility to man that post

1503
02:00:23,259 --> 02:00:28,058
and not allow Islam to be attacked from where you are appointed

1504
02:00:29,377 --> 02:00:34,345
and don't change that post just because you don't feel like doing it do what pleases Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1505
02:00:34,913 --> 02:00:40,355
So he told him: You should not do what you love, but you should do what Allah loves.

1506
02:00:40,759 --> 02:00:46,592
O Dharar(ضرار), Don't you know that the Messenger of Allah only made Hajj(حَجْ) once,

1507
02:00:46,892 --> 02:00:50,042
but then he spent his life fighting in Jihad(جهاد) until he met Allah.

1508
02:00:51,665 --> 02:00:57,023
O Dharar(ضرار), if you make Hajj(حَجْ), then you are rewarded for your Hajj(حَجْ) and Umrah(عمرة).

1509
02:00:57,705 --> 02:01:03,255
But if you are posted in Jihad(جهاد) or fighting and protecting the backs of Muslims,

1510
02:01:03,555 --> 02:01:07,374
then if the house is visited by 100,000 pilgrims,

1511
02:01:07,630 --> 02:01:12,715
or whatever number you would be getting the reward of every one of their Hajj(حَجْ)

1512
02:01:13,015 --> 02:01:17,577
and the Hajj(حَجْ) of every believing man or woman, until the day of judgment.

1513
02:01:18,069 --> 02:01:21,992
Because whoever protects the believers is like the one who protects them,

1514
02:01:22,242 --> 02:01:24,635
from the time of Adam(آدم) until the Day of Judgment.

1515
02:01:26,026 --> 02:01:29,303
These people are only making Hajj(حَجْ), because you are protecting them.

1516
02:01:29,703 --> 02:01:32,216
Therefore you will have a share in every Hajj(حَجْ) that they make.

1517
02:01:34,237 --> 02:01:41,546
And then he says,: You are also rewarded for fighting the non believers from the day of Adam(آدم), until the day of judgment,

1518
02:01:41,834 --> 02:01:47,026
because whoever fights them today is like the one, who fights them from the day Adam(آدم) was created,

1519
02:01:47,226 --> 02:01:48,462
until the day of judgment.

1520
02:01:48,911 --> 02:01:54,599
You are also rewarded for every letter revealed in the Torah(تولراة), gospel and Qur'an

1521
02:01:54,763 --> 02:01:58,635
because you are fighting to protect the light of Allah, from being extinguished.

1522
02:01:59,701 --> 02:02:00,808
O Dharar Bin Amr(ضراربن عمرو),

1523
02:02:01,991 --> 02:02:08,884
Don't you know that there is no one closer to the status of prophethood, than the scholars of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

1524
02:02:09,415 --> 02:02:10,560
I said: And how's that.

1525
02:02:11,008 --> 02:02:16,787
He said, because the scholars are the ones, who fulfill the role of the prophets in guiding others to the truth,

1526
02:02:17,087 --> 02:02:18,168
and teaching it to them.

1527
02:02:18,468 --> 02:02:22,565
While the Mujahideen(مجاهدين), are the ones, who fight for what the prophets have brought

1528
02:02:22,951 --> 02:02:28,266
and strive to make the word of Allah, the highest and the word of the non believers, the lowest.

1529
02:02:28,789 --> 02:02:34,635
Dharar(ضرار) said: I decided to give up Hajj(حَجْ) and remain in Jihad(جهاد), until I die and meet Allah.

1530
02:02:37,505 --> 02:02:37,974
Tayeb(طيِّب),

1531
02:02:38,506 --> 02:02:42,695
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

1532
02:02:42,895 --> 02:02:44,411
If you have any questions.

1533
02:02:46,020 --> 02:02:49,207
We should gear everything that we do towards the service of religion.

1534
02:02:52,852 --> 02:02:58,527
And if the venue of Jihad(جهاد) is not open today it will be open tomorrow.

1535
02:03:01,521 --> 02:03:05,411
Therefore, no time is wasted.

1536
02:03:06,236 --> 02:03:11,133
Because the preparation for Jihad(جهاد) is Jihad(جهاد). And

1537
02:03:11,233 --> 02:03:14,279
مال يتم الواجب ، إلَّا به فهو واجب

1538
02:03:16,635 --> 02:03:19,806
The things that lead to something that is wajib(واجب) are also wajib(واجب).

1539
02:03:20,818 --> 02:03:25,668
If the wajib(واجب) is based on some prerequisites, those prerequisites become wajib(واجب).

1540
02:03:26,854 --> 02:03:30,318
So, we don't have any time to waste or spare.

1541
02:03:31,760 --> 02:03:36,871
We need the Eeman(ايمان) preparation, financial preparation, physical preparation, mental preparation.

1542
02:03:37,007 --> 02:03:45,522
You know to get yourself into the mental status of willing to leave.

1543
02:03:46,725 --> 02:03:47,932
Leave behind everything.

1544
02:03:48,132 --> 02:03:56,338
That in itself takes some preparation to get yourself to that state, where, when the call of

1545
02:03:56,430 --> 02:03:57,386
حيَّ على الجهاد

1546
02:03:57,457 --> 02:04:00,612
comes, I'm immediately going to respond to it.

1547
02:04:01,315 --> 02:04:06,965
Because in the time of Fitan(فتن) and when the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) hits.

1548
02:04:08,568 --> 02:04:14,139
If you are not ready for it from before you cannot be ready for it after there's no time for preparation after it.

1549
02:04:14,339 --> 02:04:19,196
To give an extreme example with Dajjal(دجال). Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

1550
02:04:19,296 --> 02:04:22,647
لَا يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا إِيمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ آمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ أَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِي إِيمَانِهَا خَيْرًا

1551
02:04:22,747 --> 02:04:24,547
And he is narrating, an Ayah(آية) in Qur'an.

1552
02:04:26,511 --> 02:04:33,397
At that time, no soul will benefit if it did not already benefit from its Eeman(ايمان) before.

1553
02:04:33,697 --> 02:04:36,929
So when the Dajjal(دجال) comes, you cannot say: I'm going to prepare for him now.

1554
02:04:37,229 --> 02:04:40,243
If you weren't already ready. You failed.

1555
02:04:41,151 --> 02:04:46,704
So, when the call comes in time of fittan(فتن) a person already needs to be ready, to face the test

1556
02:04:46,804 --> 02:04:50,338
because there is no time for preparation for the test and you cannot cram it, the evening before.

1557
02:04:51,557 --> 02:05:01,187
Therefore, there's a lot to be done, and brothers should not be edgy or in a hurry and to hasten things.

1558
02:05:02,046 --> 02:05:06,298
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has a plan and the Rayah(راية) of Jihad(جهاد) will never stop.

1559
02:05:07,170 --> 02:05:10,477
If it stops in one place, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ opens it somewhere else.

1560
02:05:11,223 --> 02:05:15,579
But the problem is that brothers waste a lot of time and when it's open, they're not ready for it.

1561
02:05:18,907 --> 02:05:22,565
Yahya bin Maeen(يحي بن معين) and Ahmed Bin Hanbal(أحمد بن حنبل) and some other scholars say

1562
02:05:22,621 --> 02:05:25,372
that Taifa-Al-Mansoorah(طائفة المنصورة) are Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث) that people of Hadith(حديث).

1563
02:05:26,103 --> 02:05:27,748
What is meant by the people of Hadith.?

1564
02:05:29,843 --> 02:05:34,710
It means that they are the people who are the closest to following the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1565
02:05:36,250 --> 02:05:38,992
It is the people who emphasize on the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

1566
02:05:40,041 --> 02:05:44,907
that is the Taifah(طائفة), it doesn't necessarily mean scholars of Hadith(حديث).

1567
02:05:46,356 --> 02:05:49,606
See At-Taifah(ألطائفة) is sometimes when it says Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث)

1568
02:05:50,060 --> 02:05:55,529
we misinterpret it because there's a group named Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث) and the scholars of Hadith(حديث)

1569
02:05:55,829 --> 02:05:59,412
we misinterpret the meaning of Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث) to mean scholars of Hadith(حديث).

1570
02:06:00,231 --> 02:06:03,801
Does that mean that scholars of Fiqh(فقه) are not Taifah(طائفة), or the Tafseer(تفسير)

1571
02:06:04,007 --> 02:06:05,304
and how comes it's scholars Hadith(حديث).

1572
02:06:05,538 --> 02:06:07,769
So, that's not the right understanding of what Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث) means.

1573
02:06:08,256 --> 02:06:10,234
Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث) means the people of Hadith(حديث),

1574
02:06:10,693 --> 02:06:16,107
the people who are following the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and trying to emulate his way in their lives,

1575
02:06:16,599 --> 02:06:20,021
which makes the Mujahideen(مجاهدين), the closest to this definition,

1576
02:06:20,257 --> 02:06:24,352
because they are the ones, who are trying their best to follow the Sunnah(سنة) Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1577
02:06:24,452 --> 02:06:31,370
Therefore you would find that it's very rare to find among Al-Mujahideen(مجاهدين), people have problems with Sunnah(سنة).

1578
02:06:34,034 --> 02:06:41,261
The whole lifestyle of Jihad(جهاد) brings you closer to the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and wanting to be like Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1579
02:06:41,861 --> 02:06:47,515
If you wanted to be like Rasool Allah ﷺ and the thing that preoccupied Rasool Allah ﷺ for his entire stay in Madina,

1580
02:06:47,815 --> 02:06:49,929
why wouldn't you want to be like him in the way he looked,

1581
02:06:50,238 --> 02:06:52,705
or the way he ate, or the issues that are much simpler.

1582
02:06:54,061 --> 02:06:59,186
So Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث) here is the people, who are trying to follow the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ in their life.

1583
02:06:59,550 --> 02:07:00,761
That's what is meant by Ahl-Ul-Hadith(أهل الحديث).

1584
02:07:01,802 --> 02:07:04,874
So it doesn't really change the time, it's same.

